BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 716.5 Td (Why the Interviewer Rejects This Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 701.5 Td (* **Time Complexity:** `.Distinct\(\)` internally allocates a `HashSet<int>`. It iterates) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 690.5 Td (  over the array and adds items to the hash set. Time complexity: $O\(N\)$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 677.5 Td (* **Space Complexity:** It allocates a hash set on the Managed Heap \($O\(N\)$ memory\) and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 666.5 Td (  then allocates a completely brand-new array via `.ToArray\(\)` \($O\(N\)$ memory\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 653.5 Td (* **Ignores Constraints:** The problem specified **in-place**. Allocating $2N$ heap memory) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 642.5 Td (  violates the fundamental requirement.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 629.5 Td (* **Hides Problem-Solving Capability:** The interviewer learns nothing about whether you) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 618.5 Td (  understand memory traversal, pointers, or loop invariants.) Tj ET
