BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 752 Td (1. How to Think) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 737 Td (Rotate an array of $N$ elements to the right by $K$ steps.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 721 Td (* **Example:** `[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]`, $K = 3 \\implies [5, 6, 7, 1, 2, 3, 4]$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 708 Td (* **Pattern Recognition:**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 695 Td (* Notice what happens to the segments: The last $K$ elements move to the front; the first) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 684 Td (  $N-K$ elements shift to the back.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 671 Td (* Can we achieve this without allocating an auxiliary array of size $N$?) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 658 Td (2. How Interviewer Thinks) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 643 Td (* Tests candidate's ability to manipulate memory in-place.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 630 Td (* Tests modular arithmetic: What if $K > N$? \($K = K \\pmod N$\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 617 Td (* Distinguishes between someone who creates a temporary array \($O\(N\)$ space\) vs. someone) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 606 Td (  who knows the Three-Step In-Place Reversal algorithm \($O\(1\)$ space\).) Tj ET
