BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 370.5 Td ($$P\(x\) \\text{ is } [\\text{False}, \\text{False}, \\dots, \\text{False}, \\mathbf{True},) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 358.5 Td (\\mathbf{True}, \\dots, \\mathbf{True}]$$) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 342.5 Td (Then Binary Search can find the **exact boundary** where False becomes True in $O\(\\log N\)$) Tj ET
