0.96 0.96 0.97 rg 45 158.0 505 55.5 re f
0.82 0.84 0.88 RG 0.5 w 45 158.0 505 55.5 re s
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 204.5 Td (   // WRONG: Can overflow int.MaxValue \(2,147,483,647\) when low + high > Int32.MaxVal) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 195.0 Td (   int mid = \(low + high\) / 2;) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 185.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 176.0 Td (   // CORRECT: Mathematically equivalent, immune to integer overflow:) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 166.5 Td (   int mid = low + \(high - low\) / 2;) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 150.0 Td (* **Loop Condition \(`low <= high` vs. `low < high`\):**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 137.0 Td (* Use `low <= high` when searching for a single target where the search space reduces to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 126.0 Td (  `low == high`. Inside, use `low = mid + 1` and `high = mid - 1`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 113.0 Td (* Use `low < high` when searching for an inflection point or boundary where `mid` can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 102.0 Td (  the answer \(`high = mid`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 89.0 Td (* **Termination Guarantee:** Every branch MUST shrink the search space by at least 1) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 78.0 Td (  element; otherwise, you risk an infinite loop.) Tj ET
