BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 274 Td ([NOTE] "When we notice a performance issue, I follow a structured diagnosis process rather) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 262 Td (than guessing:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 246 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 230 Td ([NOTE] **Step 1: Measure first, optimize second.**) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 214 Td ([NOTE] We never optimize without data. We look at metrics first: response time percentiles) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 202 Td (\(p95, p99\), error rates, database query duration, memory usage. Application Insights gives us) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 190 Td (transaction traces so we can see exactly which part of the request is slow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 174 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 158 Td ([NOTE] **Step 2: Identify the bottleneck.**) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 142 Td ([NOTE] Is it CPU? Memory? Database? External API? Network? Usually it's one of:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 126 Td ([NOTE] - **N+1 queries** - loading related data in a loop instead of a single JOIN) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 110 Td ([NOTE] - **Missing database index** - full table scans on large tables) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 94 Td ([NOTE] - **No caching** - expensive computations or queries repeated unnecessarily) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 78 Td ([NOTE] - **Synchronous blocking** - thread pool starvation from blocking async code) Tj ET
