BT /F2 11.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.25 rg 45 754 Td (8. API SECURITY DEEP DIVE) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 736 Td (Complete Script: "How do you ensure API security?") Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 721 Td ([NOTE] "API security is layered - there's no single control. We implement defense in depth:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 705 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 689 Td ([NOTE] **1. Authentication & Authorization:**) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 673 Td ([NOTE] JWT authentication validates every request. Role-based and policy-based authorization) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 661 Td (controls what authenticated users can do. We follow least-privilege - users get only what they) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 649 Td (need.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 633 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 617 Td ([NOTE] **2. Input Validation:**) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 601 Td ([NOTE] Every incoming DTO is validated with FluentValidation. We validate data types, ranges,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 589 Td (length limits, and format \(regex for emails, etc.\). We never trust client input - SQL injection) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 577 Td (is impossible with parameterized queries \(EF Core does this by default\), but we still validate) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 565 Td (to protect business logic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 549 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 533 Td ([NOTE] **3. Rate Limiting:**) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 517 Td ([NOTE] We use ASP.NET Core's built-in rate limiting middleware \(introduced in .NET 7\) to limit) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 505 Td (requests per client per window. This prevents brute-force attacks on login and DoS attacks on) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 493 Td (expensive endpoints. For distributed rate limiting across instances, we back the counter with) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 481 Td (Redis.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 465 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 449 Td ([NOTE] **4. CORS:**) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 433 Td ([NOTE] We configure CORS explicitly - only allowed origins can make cross-origin requests. We) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 421 Td (never use wildcard \(`*`\) in production.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 405 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 389 Td ([NOTE] **5. HTTPS Everywhere:**) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 373 Td ([NOTE] All traffic is HTTPS. We use HSTS to instruct browsers to only connect over HTTPS. In) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 361 Td (development we use the developer cert; in production we use a proper TLS certificate \(ACM in) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 349 Td (AWS or Let's Encrypt\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 333 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 317 Td ([NOTE] **6. Security Headers:**) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 301 Td ([NOTE] We add security headers via middleware: `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 289 Td (`X-Frame-Options: DENY`, `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`. We configure Content Security Policy) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 277 Td (for any web-facing responses.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 261 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 245 Td ([NOTE] **7. Secret Management:**) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 229 Td ([NOTE] No secrets in code or appsettings.json committed to source control. We use Azure Key) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 217 Td (Vault \(or AWS Secrets Manager\) for production secrets, accessed via the `IConfiguration`) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 205 Td (abstraction. Locally, we use .NET User Secrets.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 189 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 173 Td ([NOTE] **8. Sensitive Data Handling:**) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 157 Td ([NOTE] Passwords are bcrypt-hashed. PII is stored encrypted at rest. Sensitive fields are) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 145 Td (excluded from logs using Serilog destructuring policies.") Tj ET
