BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 724 Td (UPDATE statements. If another user has modified the record, the update affects 0 rows, and EF) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 712 Td (Core throws `DbUpdateConcurrencyException`. We catch this, reload the entity, and either) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 700 Td (auto-merge or surface a conflict to the user.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 684 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 668 Td ([NOTE] ```csharp) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 652 Td ([NOTE] [Timestamp]) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 636 Td ([NOTE] public byte[] RowVersion { get; set; }) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 620 Td ([NOTE] ```) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 604 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 588 Td ([NOTE] **2. Database Transactions:**) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 572 Td ([NOTE] When multiple database operations must succeed or fail together, we use explicit) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 560 Td (transactions:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 544 Td ([NOTE] ```csharp) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 528 Td ([NOTE] using var transaction = await _context.Database.BeginTransactionAsync\(\);) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 512 Td ([NOTE] try) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 496 Td ([NOTE] {) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 480 Td ([NOTE] // Multiple operations) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 464 Td ([NOTE] await _context.SaveChangesAsync\(\);) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 448 Td ([NOTE] await transaction.CommitAsync\(\);) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 432 Td ([NOTE] }) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 416 Td ([NOTE] catch { await transaction.RollbackAsync\(\); throw; }) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 400 Td ([NOTE] ```) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 384 Td ([NOTE] We choose the appropriate isolation level: `ReadCommitted` \(default, prevents dirty) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 372 Td (reads\), `RepeatableRead` \(prevents non-repeatable reads\), `Serializable` \(prevents phantom) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 360 Td (reads but has highest contention\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 344 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 328 Td ([NOTE] **3. Distributed Locking with Redis:**) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 312 Td ([NOTE] For distributed scenarios - multiple instances of our service running simultaneously -) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 300 Td (database transactions aren't enough for non-database operations. We use Redis distributed lock) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 288 Td (\(RedLock algorithm\) to ensure only one instance processes a critical section at a time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 272 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 256 Td ([NOTE] Example: Processing a payment - we don't want two instances to process the same payment) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 244 Td (simultaneously. We acquire a Redis lock on the payment ID before processing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 228 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 212 Td ([NOTE] **4. Async Concurrency - Semaphores:**) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 196 Td ([NOTE] Within a single process, if we need to limit concurrent access to a resource, we use) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 184 Td (`SemaphoreSlim`:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 168 Td ([NOTE] ```csharp) Tj ET
