BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (  primitive blittable value types without padding, it uses native bitwise comparison\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 767 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 751 Td (Q005: Static Constructors \(`.cctor`\) Execution Guarantees and Failure Modes) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 736 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 723 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 710 Td (* A static constructor \(represented as `.cctor` in IL\) initializes type-level state.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 697 Td (* **Execution Guarantees**: Guaranteed by the CLR to run exactly once per `AppDomain`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 686 Td (  before any instance of the class is created or any static members are accessed. It is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 675 Td (  thread-safe; the CLR acquires an internal lock during initial invocation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 662 Td (* It takes no parameters, has no access modifiers \(`public`/`private`\), and cannot be) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 651 Td (  called directly by user code.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 638 Td (* **Catastrophic Failure Mode**: If an unhandled exception is thrown inside a static) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 627 Td (  constructor, the CLR wraps it in a `TypeInitializationException`. The type becomes) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 616 Td (  permanently unusable for the remaining lifetime of the `AppDomain`. Any subsequent attempt) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 605 Td (  to access the type immediately throws `TypeInitializationException` without re-executing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 594 Td (  the constructor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 581 Td (* **The Trap**: Catching the exception inside calling code and assuming subsequent calls) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 570 Td (  will succeed. Once a static constructor fails, the type is poisoned permanently until) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 559 Td (  process/domain restart.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 546 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What is the difference in CLR initialization timing between a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 535 Td (  class with an explicit static constructor vs a class that initializes static fields inline) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 524 Td (  without an explicit constructor? *\(Answer: Inline field initialization marks the class) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 513 Td (  with the `beforefieldinit` IL metadata flag, allowing the JIT compiler to run) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 502 Td (  initialization lazily at any time before the first static field access. An explicit static) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 491 Td (  constructor removes `beforefieldinit`, enforcing strict initialization immediately before) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 480 Td (  the first member access or instantiation\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 467 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 451 Td (Q006: `const` vs `readonly` vs `static readonly`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 436 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Basic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 423 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 410 Td (* **`const`**: Compile-time constant. Evaluated at compile time; the compiler burns the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 399 Td (  literal value directly into the calling assembly's IL code \(call site inlining\). Can only) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 388 Td (  be applied to primitive types, enums, or strings.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 375 Td (* **`readonly`**: Runtime constant. Evaluated at runtime. Can only be initialized at the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 364 Td (  declaration line or within an instance constructor. Holds complex objects and allocations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 351 Td (* **`static readonly`**: Initialized during type loading \(static constructor\). Shared) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 340 Td (  across all instances of the type, cannot be modified after `.cctor` completion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 327 Td (* **The Trap**: Exposing `public const` across library/assembly boundaries. If Library A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 316 Td (  changes `public const int MaxRetry = 5` to `10`, and Application B references Library A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 305 Td (  without being recompiled, Application B continues using `5` because the value was inlined) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 294 Td (  into its IL at build time. Use `public static readonly` across assemblies.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 281 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: Can a `readonly` field's state be mutated if it holds a reference) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 270 Td (  type? *\(Answer: Yes. The reference pointer itself is immutable and cannot be redirected to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 259 Td (  a new object, but the internal state/properties of the referenced object on the heap can) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 248 Td (  be freely mutated\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 235 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 219 Td (Q007: Nullable Reference Types \(NRT\) Mechanics and Runtime Realities) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 204 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 191 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 178 Td (* Introduced in C# 8.0 to combat `NullReferenceException`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 165 Td (* **Compile-time Construct Only**: NRT \(`string?` vs `string`\) is entirely a static) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 154 Td (  compiler analysis tool. At runtime, both `string?` and `string` are identical: a standard) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 143 Td (  CLI reference pointer that can physically be `null`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 130 Td (* The compiler emits metadata attributes \(`[Nullable]`, `[NullableContext]`\) into) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 119 Td (  assemblies to inform consuming code of nullability contracts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 106 Td (* The null-forgiving operator \(`!`\) tells the compiler to suppress warnings, but provides) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 95 Td (  zero runtime null-checking.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 82 Td (* **The Trap**: Assuming that using `string` \(non-nullable\) guarantees at runtime that the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 71 Td (  parameter will never be null. Deserializing malformed JSON, reflection, or un-annotated) Tj ET
