BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (* **Gen 0**: Ephemeral, short-lived objects \(temporary allocations, local variables, DTOs\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 769 Td (  Smallest budget; collected frequently \(sub-millisecond\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 756 Td (* **Gen 1**: Buffer generation between short-lived and long-lived objects.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 743 Td (* **Gen 2**: Long-lived objects \(singletons, static caches, AppContext, long-running) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 732 Td (  connections\). Collected infrequently via full GC.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 719 Td (* **GC Roots**: Starting points for reachability graphs: CPU registers, active stack local) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 708 Td (  variables/parameters, static fields, GC handles \(`GCHandle`\), and finalization queues.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 695 Td (* **Collection Triggers**: Allocation budget exceeded for a generation, explicit call to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 684 Td (  `GC.Collect\(\)`, low physical memory notification from the OS, or unloading an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 673 Td (  `AssemblyLoadContext`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 660 Td (* **The Trap**: Believing that calling `GC.Collect\(\)` improves application performance. In) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 649 Td (  production, calling `GC.Collect\(\)` forces a Gen 2 sweep, halts application threads) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 638 Td (  \(Stop-The-World pause\), ruins generation balancing algorithms, and degrades throughput.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 625 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What are the Large Object Heap \(LOH\) and Pinned Object Heap) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 614 Td (  \(POH\), and what thresholds apply? *\(Answer: Objects $\\ge$ 85,000 bytes go directly to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 603 Td (  LOH. The POH, introduced in .NET 5, holds objects pinned for native interop to avoid SOH) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 592 Td (  fragmentation. Both are collected during Gen 2 collections\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 579 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 563 Td (Q011: The Standard Dispose Pattern and `SafeHandle`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 548 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 535 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 522 Td (* The Dispose pattern standardizes deterministic resource cleanup for unmanaged resources) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 511 Td (  \(database handles, OS file descriptors, sockets\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 498 Td (* Implements `IDisposable` with `Dispose\(\)` and `protected virtual void Dispose\(bool) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 487 Td (  disposing\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 474 Td (* **The Mechanics of `disposing` parameter**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 461 Td (* When `disposing == true`: Invoked explicitly via user code \(`Dispose\(\)` or `using`\). Safe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 450 Td (  to release both managed resources \(other disposable objects\) and unmanaged resources.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 437 Td (* When `disposing == false`: Invoked by the runtime Finalizer \(`~MyClass\(\)`\). **Unsafe** to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 426 Td (  access managed objects because they may have already been finalized or collected. Only) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 415 Td (  unmanaged native pointers should be freed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 402 Td (* Calls `GC.SuppressFinalize\(this\)` to tell the GC that cleanup is complete, removing the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 391 Td (  object from the Finalization Queue and avoiding Gen 2 resurrection costs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 378 Td (* Modern best practice: Encapsulate unmanaged handles in `SafeHandle` \(e.g.,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 367 Td (  `SafeFileHandle`\), which guarantees leak-free cleanup even under asynchronous thread) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 356 Td (  aborts without requiring custom finalizers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 343 Td (* **The Trap**: Writing finalizers \(`~ClassName\(\)`\) on classes that only hold managed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 332 Td (  disposable dependencies \(like `HttpClient` or `SqlConnection`\). This moves the object into) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 321 Td (  Gen 2 and drastically increases GC overhead. Finalizers should *only* exist when holding) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 310 Td (  raw `IntPtr` native resources directly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 297 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does `IAsyncDisposable` with `DisposeAsync\(\)` differ from) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 286 Td (  `IDisposable`, and when must you use it? *\(Answer: `DisposeAsync` enables flushing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 275 Td (  asynchronous network streams, completing disk writes, and returning pooled connections) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 264 Td (  asynchronously without blocking calling threads on OS I/O\).*) Tj ET
