BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 220 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Basic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 207 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 194 Td (* **`is`**: Checks if an object is compatible with a given type. Returns `bool`. Modern C#) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 183 Td (  supports declaration pattern matching: `if \(obj is OrderService svc\) { svc.Process\(\); }`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 172 Td (  which tests and casts in a single instruction without double evaluation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 159 Td (* **`as`**: Performs an explicit reference conversion or nullable conversion. Returns the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 148 Td (  typed reference if successful, or `null` if the cast fails. It never throws) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 137 Td (  `InvalidCastException`. Cannot be used on non-nullable value types.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 124 Td (* Performance: The historical anti-pattern `if \(obj is Type\) { var x = \(Type\)obj; }`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 113 Td (  incurred two CLR type checks. Modern pattern matching `if \(obj is Type t\)` compiles down) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 102 Td (  to a single type-check instruction \(`isinst`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 89 Td (* **The Trap**: Using `as` on non-nullable value types \(e.g., `obj as int`\), which produces) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 78 Td (  a compiler error because `int` cannot be null \(must use `obj as int?`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 65 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does C# 9+ switch pattern matching handle relational and) Tj ET
