BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 707 Td (Q016: CLR Generics Implementation: Specialization vs Sharing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 692 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 679 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 666 Td (* Unlike C++ templates \(which generate separate assembly code for every type argument at) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 655 Td (  compile time\) or Java generics \(which use type erasure and treat everything as `Object`\),) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 644 Td (  C# generics are preserved as first-class citizens in metadata and evaluated at JIT) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 633 Td (  compilation time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 620 Td (* **Value Types \(Specialization\)**: The JIT compiler generates unique native machine code) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 609 Td (  for each distinct value type \(e.g., `List<int>` vs `List<double>`\). Because value types) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 598 Td (  have different byte sizes and memory layouts, specialized machine code ensures maximum CPU) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 587 Td (  register utilization and eliminates boxing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 574 Td (* **Reference Types \(Code Sharing\)**: The JIT compiler generates exactly one shared native) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 563 Td (  machine code implementation for all reference types \(e.g., `List<string>`, `List<Order>`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 552 Td (  `List<Customer>`\). Since all reference pointers are identical in size \(8 bytes on 64-bit) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 541 Td (  systems\) and managed identically by the GC, sharing machine code drastically reduces) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 530 Td (  memory footprint and JIT compilation time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 517 Td (* **The Trap**: Assuming `List<int>` and `List<string>` share native machine code under the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 506 Td (  hood. Value types never share machine code with other types.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 493 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What is the impact of generic static fields \(e.g., `class) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 482 Td (  Cache<T> { public static int Count; }`\)? *\(Answer: Every unique closed generic type gets) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 471 Td (  its own independent static field instance: `Cache<int>.Count` is completely isolated from) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 460 Td (  `Cache<string>.Count`\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 447 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 431 Td (Q017: Generic Variance: Covariance \(`out`\) vs Contravariance \(`in`\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 416 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 403 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 390 Td (* Variance defines how subtyping between more complex types relates to subtyping between) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 379 Td (  their component types. Only applies to generic interfaces and generic delegates; never to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 368 Td (  classes or structs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 355 Td (* **Covariance \(`out T`\)**: Preserves inheritance direction. Allows assigning a more) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 344 Td (  derived type to a less derived reference. E.g., `IEnumerable<out T>` allows assigning) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 333 Td (  `IEnumerable<Derived>` to `IEnumerable<Base>`. Restricts `T` to appear only in method) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 322 Td (  return/output positions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 309 Td (* **Contravariance \(`in T`\)**: Reverses inheritance direction. Allows assigning a less) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 298 Td (  derived type to a more derived reference. E.g., `Action<in T>` or `IComparer<in T>` allows) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 287 Td (  assigning `IComparer<Base>` to `IComparer<Derived>`. Restricts `T` to appear only in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 276 Td (  method parameter/input positions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 263 Td (* **Invariance**: Default behavior. Generic type parameters without `in`/`out` require) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 252 Td (  exact type matches \(e.g., `IList<T>`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 239 Td (* **The Trap**: Trying to make `IList<T>` covariant. If `IList<Animal> animals = new) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 228 Td (  List<Dog>\(\)` were allowed, you could execute `animals.Add\(new Cat\(\)\)`, corrupting type) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 217 Td (  safety at runtime.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 204 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: Can generic variance be used with value types \(e.g., converting) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 193 Td (  `IEnumerable<int>` to `IEnumerable<object>`\)? *\(Answer: No. Variance only applies to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 182 Td (  reference conversions. Value types require memory transformation/boxing, which is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 171 Td (  prohibited in generic variance\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 158 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 142 Td (Q018: Delegates vs Events and Delegate Memory Leaks) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 127 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 114 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 101 Td (* **Delegate**: A type-safe, object-oriented function pointer. Under the hood, inherits) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 90 Td (  from `System.MulticastDelegate` \(which derives from `System.Delegate`\). Contains two) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 79 Td (  primary private pointers: `_target` \(the object instance\) and `_methodPtr` \(the native) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 68 Td (  function address\), plus an invocation list `_invocationList`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.4 0.4 0.4 rg
45 25 Td (INFOSYS & ENTERPRISE .NET INTERVIEW PREPARATION GUIDE  |  Page 67) Tj ET
