BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 780 Td (Q021: Expression Trees vs Compiled Delegates) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 765 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 752 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 739 Td (* `Func<T, bool>` is a compiled IL delegate that executes directly on the CPU evaluation) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 728 Td (  stack.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 715 Td (* `Expression<Func<T, bool>>` is a data structure \(Abstract Syntax Tree / AST\) representing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 704 Td (  the code logic. Nodes represent binary expressions, member accesses, constants, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 693 Td (  parameter calls.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 680 Td (* The compiler parses the lambda and emits code to construct nodes: `Expression.Lambda`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 669 Td (  `Expression.Equal`, `Expression.Property`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 656 Td (* Providers like EF Core traverse this tree at runtime to translate C# logic into SQL) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 645 Td (  `WHERE` clauses.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 632 Td (* Expression trees can be compiled into native delegates at runtime via `.Compile\(\)`, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 621 Td (  compilation is extremely CPU-expensive and should be cached if reused.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 608 Td (* **The Trap**: Passing a method call that cannot be translated into an Expression Tree in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 597 Td (  an EF Core query \(e.g., `Where\(x => CustomMethod\(x.Id\)\)`\), which will throw runtime) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 586 Td (  translation exceptions in modern EF Core.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 573 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: Why does `Expression.Compile\(\)` have a high CPU cost, and how) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 562 Td (  does the Dapper library achieve fast mapping without it? *\(Answer: `.Compile\(\)` invokes) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 551 Td (  the runtime JIT compiler to generate a DynamicMethod and emit IL; Dapper uses lightweight) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 540 Td (  IL emit \(`ILGenerator`\) and caches the emitted delegates by SQL query hash\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 527 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 511 Td (Q022: `Span<T>` and `ReadOnlySpan<T>` Internals and Memory Safety) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 496 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 483 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 470 Td (* `Span<T>` is a `ref struct` representing a contiguous region of arbitrary memory \(Managed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 459 Td (  Heap arrays, Stack-allocated buffers via `stackalloc`, or Unmanaged native heap memory\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 446 Td (* Internally defined as a **ByReference** pointer and an integer length:) Tj ET
