BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 705 Td (Q032: Cancellation Tokens Architecture and Linked Tokens) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 690 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 677 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 664 Td (* Asynchronous cooperative cancellation uses two classes: `CancellationTokenSource` \(CTS -) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 653 Td (  producer/signaler\) and `CancellationToken` \(CT - consumer/listener\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 640 Td (* **Cooperative**: Operations are not aborted forcibly. The executing code must poll) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 629 Td (  `token.IsCancellationRequested`, call `token.ThrowIfCancellationRequested\(\)`, or pass the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 618 Td (  token to asynchronous BCL APIs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 605 Td (* **Linked Tokens**: `CancellationTokenSource.CreateLinkedTokenSource\(token1, token2\)`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 594 Td (  creates a composite CTS that signals cancellation if *either* token cancels \(e.g.,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 583 Td (  combining a client disconnect token with a 5-second timeout CTS\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 570 Td (* Memory Warning: A linked CTS registers callbacks on the parent tokens. If parent tokens) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 559 Td (  are long-lived, you must explicitly `Dispose\(\)` the linked CTS to unregister callbacks and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 548 Td (  prevent memory leaks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 535 Td (* **The Trap**: Catching generic `Exception` inside a method and suppressing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 524 Td (  `OperationCanceledException` / `TaskCanceledException`, preventing upstream controllers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 513 Td (  from properly returning HTTP 499 / 503.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 500 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does ASP.NET Core expose client disconnects via cancellation) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 489 Td (  tokens? *\(Answer: Through `HttpContext.RequestAborted`, which fires when the HTTP client) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 478 Td (  terminates the TCP connection before the server finishes streaming the response\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 465 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 449 Td (Q033: Unsafe Code, Pointers, and Fixed Memory) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 434 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 421 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 408 Td (* Code marked `unsafe` allows direct pointer manipulation \(`*`, `&`, `->`\) bypassing CLR) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 397 Td (  type safety.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 384 Td (* **`fixed` Statement**: Instructs the GC to **pin** a managed object at its current memory) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 373 Td (  address on the Managed Heap. Without pinning, the GC can move objects during compaction,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 362 Td (  turning raw pointers into invalid dangling pointers that cause memory corruption or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 351 Td (  segmentation faults.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 338 Td (* Used in high-performance native interop \(P/Invoke\) and ultra-fast byte transformations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 325 Td (* **The Trap**: Leaving managed objects pinned for extended periods. Pinned objects) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 314 Td (  fragment the Small Object Heap \(SOH\) by creating immovable roadblocks for GC compaction.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 301 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does modern .NET avoid the need for `unsafe` and pinning for) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 290 Td (  array/string manipulation? *\(Answer: Through `Span<T>`, `ReadOnlySpan<T>`, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 279 Td (  `MemoryMarshal`, which provide memory safety while delivering direct native-like pointer) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 268 Td (  performance\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 255 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 239 Td (Q034: AssemblyLoadContext and Dynamic Plugin Architecture) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 224 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 211 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 198 Td (* Prior to .NET Core, `AppDomain` was the boundary for isolation and unloading. Modern .NET) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 187 Td (  uses `AssemblyLoadContext` \(ALC\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 174 Td (* ALCs provide dependency isolation: two plugins can load different, conflicting versions) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 163 Td (  of the same assembly \(e.g., `Newtonsoft.Json` 12 vs 13\) within the same process.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 150 Td (* **Collectible ALCs**: An ALC created with `isCollectible: true` can be completely) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 139 Td (  unloaded, allowing assemblies to be removed from memory.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 126 Td (* For unloading to succeed, **every** reference to types, objects, and metadata originating) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 115 Td (  from the ALC must be cleared; otherwise, the context remains in memory.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 102 Td (* **The Trap**: Passing an object instantiated from a collectible ALC into a static cache) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 91 Td (  in the host application, permanently blocking the entire ALC from being garbage collected.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 78 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How do you verify that an `AssemblyLoadContext` has successfully) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 67 Td (  unloaded? *\(Answer: Wrap the reference in a `WeakReference`, invoke `.Unload\(\)`, run a Gen) Tj ET
