BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 751 Td (Q035: Source Generators vs Reflection: Performance and AOT) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 736 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 723 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 710 Td (* **Reflection**: Examines assembly metadata at runtime \(`System.Type`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 699 Td (  `MethodInfo.Invoke`\). Dynamic, flexible, but computationally expensive: prevents) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 688 Td (  compile-time optimization, causes allocations, and cannot be statically analyzed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 675 Td (* **Roslyn Source Generators**: Run during compilation. They inspect user code syntax and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 664 Td (  semantics via Roslyn APIs and generate additional C# source files directly into the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 653 Td (  compilation pipeline.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 640 Td (* **Native AOT \(Ahead-Of-Time\)**: In modern .NET \(8/9\), Native AOT compiles C# directly) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 629 Td (  into platform-specific machine code without a JIT compiler. Unbounded runtime reflection) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 618 Td (  breaks Native AOT because the linker trims unused code. Source generators \(e.g.,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 607 Td (  `System.Text.Json` source generator\) resolve mapping at compile time, ensuring 100% Native) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 596 Td (  AOT compatibility.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 583 Td (* **The Trap**: Assuming source generators can modify existing user code. Source generators) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 572 Td (  can only *add* new code \(e.g., partial classes/methods\); they can never alter or rewrite) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 561 Td (  existing code.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 548 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does `[JsonSerializable]` source generation reduce startup) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 537 Td (  time and memory footprint in ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs? *\(Answer: It generates static) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 526 Td (  serializer/deserializer code ahead of time, eliminating the warm-up reflection cost and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 515 Td (  dynamic IL emit that happens during the first JSON request\).*) Tj ET
