BT /F2 11.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.25 rg 45 476 Td (CATEGORY 3: ASP.NET CORE ARCHITECTURE) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 458 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 442 Td (Q036: Kestrel Web Server Architecture and Transport Mechanics) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 427 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 414 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 401 Td (* Kestrel is the cross-platform, high-performance web server default for ASP.NET Core.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 390 Td (  Built on modern asynchronous I/O abstractions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 377 Td (* **Socket Transport Layer**: Replaced Libuv with managed `System.IO.Pipelines` and managed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 366 Td (  socket transports. Uses platform-native event multiplexing: I/O Completion Ports \(IOCP\) on) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 355 Td (  Windows, `epoll` on Linux, and `kqueue` on macOS.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 342 Td (* **`System.IO.Pipelines`**: Eliminates buffer copying by allocating memory directly in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 331 Td (  unmanaged or pinned memory pools \(`MemoryPool<byte>`\), parsing HTTP headers and payloads) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 320 Td (  zero-copy using `ReadOnlySequence<byte>` and `Span<byte>`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 307 Td (* **Reverse Proxy Topology**: In enterprise production, Kestrel is typically deployed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 296 Td (  behind a reverse proxy \(IIS, Nginx, YARP, Azure Front Door, AWS ALB\) for SSL termination,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 285 Td (  request filtering, edge caching, and public IP port sharing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 272 Td (* **The Trap**: Believing Kestrel cannot be exposed directly to the internet. Modern) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 261 Td (  Kestrel is hardened and enterprise-ready for direct internet exposure \(HTTP/2, HTTP/3,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 250 Td (  QUIC, TLS SNI\). However, edge features \(WAF, Geo-blocking\) often necessitate a fronting) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 239 Td (  reverse proxy.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 226 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What happens if an unhandled exception escapes all middleware in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 215 Td (  the Kestrel pipeline? *\(Answer: Kestrel logs a critical diagnostic event, returns a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 204 Td (  generic HTTP 500 Internal Server Error, and closes the TCP stream if the response has) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 193 Td (  already begun streaming\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 180 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 164 Td (Q037: `HttpContext` Lifecycle and Asynchronous Thread Safety) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 149 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 136 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 123 Td (* `HttpContext` encapsulates all HTTP-specific information \(Request, Response, User, Items,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 112 Td (  Features\) for a single HTTP transaction.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 99 Td (* **Lifecycle**: Created when a request is received by the server and disposed when the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 88 Td (  HTTP response completes. Managed within an `IServiceScope`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 75 Td (* **Thread-Safety**: `HttpContext` is **NOT** thread-safe. Multiple threads cannot read or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 64 Td (  write to `HttpContext` concurrently.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.4 0.4 0.4 rg
