BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (* Spawning background threads \(`Task.Run`\) that accept `HttpContext` as a parameter leads) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 769 Td (  to race conditions, `ObjectDisposedException`, or corrupted response streams when the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 758 Td (  original HTTP request finishes and disposes the context.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 745 Td (* **Best Practice for Background Work**: Extract required data values \(UserId, claims,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 734 Td (  request body parameters\) into local primitives/DTOs *before* kicking off background work,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 723 Td (  or resolve a fresh `IServiceScope` via `IServiceScopeFactory`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 710 Td (* **The Trap**: Passing `HttpContext` into a fire-and-forget `Task.Run` to do async) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 699 Td (  auditing. Once the parent controller returns, `HttpContext` is recycled/disposed, causing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 688 Td (  random crashes in production.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 675 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does `IHttpContextAccessor` work under the hood, and what is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 664 Td (  its performance overhead? *\(Answer: It uses `AsyncLocal<HttpContext>` to flow the context) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 653 Td (  across asynchronous awaits; accessing it adds minor lookup overhead and should not be used) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 642 Td (  in tight loops\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 629 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 613 Td (Q038: Middleware Pipeline Execution and Short-Circuiting) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 598 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Basic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 585 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 572 Td (* The ASP.NET Core request pipeline consists of a sequence of middleware delegates executed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 561 Td (  in a bidirectional "Russian Doll" or pipeline model.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 548 Td (* Registered in `Program.cs` via `app.Use...\(\)`. The order of registration strictly) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 537 Td (  dictates execution order.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 524 Td (* **Request Flow**: Each middleware executes logic on the way in, invokes the `next\(\)`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 513 Td (  delegate to pass control to the subsequent middleware, and executes logic on the way out) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 502 Td (  after downstream components complete.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 489 Td (* **Short-Circuiting**: If a middleware handles the request and does *not* invoke `await) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 478 Td (  next\(\)`, the pipeline execution terminates immediately, and the response flows backward) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 467 Td (  through the preceding middlewares \(e.g., Static File middleware serving an image,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 456 Td (  Authorization middleware returning HTTP 401/403\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 443 Td (* **The Trap**: Registering middleware in the wrong order. E.g., placing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 432 Td (  `app.UseAuthorization\(\)` before `app.UseAuthentication\(\)`, which leads to authorization) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 421 Td (  checks running against an unauthenticated `Anonymous` principal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 408 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What happens if a middleware attempts to modify response headers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 397 Td (  after calling `await next\(\)` when downstream components have already started writing to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 386 Td (  the response body? *\(Answer: Throws `InvalidOperationException: Headers are read-only,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 375 Td (  response has already started`\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 362 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 346 Td (Q039: The Captive Dependency Trap in Dependency Injection) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 331 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 318 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 305 Td (* A **Captive Dependency** occurs when a service with a longer lifetime captures a service) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 294 Td (  with a shorter lifetime as a dependency.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 281 Td (* Classic Example: Injecting a **Scoped** service \(e.g., `DbContext` or `IOrderRepository`\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 270 Td (  into a **Singleton** service \(e.g., `CacheManager` or `BackgroundService`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 257 Td (* **Catastrophic Impact**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 244 Td (* The Scoped service is instantiated once when the Singleton is resolved and remains held) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 233 Td (  in memory for the entire application lifetime.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 220 Td (* Any subsequent HTTP request calling the Singleton interacts with that *same original*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 209 Td (  Scoped instance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 196 Td (* For `DbContext`, this causes cross-request concurrency exceptions \(`A second operation) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 185 Td (  was started on this context instance before a previous operation completed`\) and memory) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 174 Td (  bloat because the DbContext change tracker grows indefinitely.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 161 Td (* ASP.NET Core has built-in validation in Development mode \(`ValidateScopes = true`\), which) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 150 Td (  throws an `InvalidOperationException` at startup if a Scoped service is resolved from) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 139 Td (  root/Singleton.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 126 Td (* **The Trap**: Disabling scope validation in production or using Service Locator) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 115 Td (  \(`serviceProvider.GetService<Scoped>\(\)`\) inside a Singleton without creating an explicit) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 104 Td (  `IServiceScope`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 91 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How do you safely consume a Scoped `DbContext` inside a Singleton) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 80 Td (  `BackgroundService`? *\(Answer: Inject `IServiceScopeFactory`, call `using var scope =) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 69 Td (  _scopeFactory.CreateScope\(\);`, and resolve the DbContext from `scope.ServiceProvider`\).*) Tj ET
