BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 780 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 764 Td (Q040: Dependency Injection Service Lifetimes: Scoped vs Transient vs Singleton) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 749 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Basic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 736 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 723 Td (* **Transient \(`AddTransient`\)**: Created every time they are requested from the container.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 712 Td (  Best for lightweight, stateless services.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 699 Td (* **Scoped \(`AddScoped`\)**: Created once per client request scope \(in ASP.NET Core, per) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 688 Td (  HTTP request\). Disposed automatically when the HTTP request ends. Best for services that) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 677 Td (  hold request-specific state, such as EF Core `DbContext`, Unit of Work, or UserContext.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 664 Td (* **Singleton \(`AddSingleton`\)**: Created on the first request \(or at startup\) and reused) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 653 Td (  across all subsequent requests for the entire lifetime of the application. Disposed only) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 642 Td (  when the application shuts down. Must be thread-safe.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 629 Td (* **Disposal Guarantee**: Any service implementing `IDisposable` or `IAsyncDisposable`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 618 Td (  resolved by the container is automatically disposed when its owning scope is disposed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 605 Td (* **The Trap**: Manually instantiating a disposable service \(`var svc = new) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 594 Td (  DisposableService\(\)`\) or resolving Transient disposable services from the Root provider) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 583 Td (  \(`app.Services.GetRequiredService<TransientDisposable>\(\)`\). The root provider holds) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 572 Td (  references until app shutdown, creating a memory leak.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 559 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: Can a Scoped service inject a Transient service? *\(Answer: Yes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 548 Td (  The Transient service is created fresh for that Scoped service and shares the Scoped) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 537 Td (  service's lifetime\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 524 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 508 Td (Q041: Controller-based APIs vs Minimal APIs Architecture) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 493 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 480 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 467 Td (* **Controller APIs**: Built on the traditional ASP.NET MVC architecture) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 456 Td (  \(`Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc`\). Relies on reflection, action invokers, model binders, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 445 Td (  action filters. Higher startup ceremony, larger memory footprint, heavier per-request) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 434 Td (  allocation overhead.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 421 Td (* **Minimal APIs** \(Introduced in .NET 6\): Built directly on top of ASP.NET Core endpoint) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 410 Td (  routing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 397 Td (* **Performance Advantage**: Bypasses MVC pipeline overhead. Compiles endpoint handlers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 386 Td (  using source-generated delegate dispatchers \(`RequestDelegateFactory`\), drastically) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 375 Td (  reducing reflection, CPU instructions, and heap allocations. Ideal for high-throughput) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 364 Td (  microservices.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 351 Td (* Feature parity: Minimal APIs support filters \(`IEndpointFilter`\), model validation,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 340 Td (  OpenAPI/Swagger annotations, and dependency injection.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 327 Td (* **The Trap**: Believing Minimal APIs cannot handle large architectures. Minimal APIs can) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 316 Td (  be cleanly organized using extension methods, Carter module pattern, or endpoint group) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 305 Td (  mapping \(`MapGroup`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 292 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How do Endpoint Filters \(`IEndpointFilter`\) differ from MVC) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 281 Td (  Action Filters? *\(Answer: Endpoint filters execute directly in the routing pipeline, wrap) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 270 Td (  arbitrary endpoint handlers including Minimal APIs, and do not carry the overhead of MVC) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 259 Td (  `ActionExecutingContext` or model state objects\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 246 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 230 Td (Q042: Action Filters vs Middleware Execution Boundaries) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 215 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 202 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 189 Td (* **Middleware**: Executes early in the ASP.NET Core pipeline. Operates at the raw HTTP) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 178 Td (  level \(`HttpContext`, Request, Response\). Completely unaware of MVC routing destinations,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 167 Td (  controller classes, model-bound objects, or executed action methods.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 154 Td (* **Action Filters**: Execute within the MVC execution pipeline *after* routing has matched) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 143 Td (  a controller action and model binding has occurred. Have rich access to `ActionContext`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 132 Td (  controller instances, action parameters, and `ModelState`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 119 Td (* **Decision Matrix**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 106 Td (* Use **Middleware** for cross-cutting global HTTP concerns: Authentication, Global) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 95 Td (  Exception handling, Request Compression, CORS, Distributed Tracing headers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 82 Td (* Use **Filters** for MVC/domain concerns: Action parameter validation, custom) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 71 Td (  authorization based on action attributes, action-specific auditing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.4 0.4 0.4 rg
