BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (* **The Trap**: Trying to validate model binding state or inspect action attributes inside) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 769 Td (  standard middleware. The middleware executes before MVC model binding has occurred.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 756 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What is the execution order between Authorization Filters,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 745 Td (  Resource Filters, Action Filters, and Result Filters? *\(Answer: Authorization Filters) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 734 Td (  $\\to$ Resource Filters \(before\) $\\to$ Action Filters \(before\) $\\to$ Action Execution $\\to$) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 723 Td (  Action Filters \(after\) $\\to$ Result Filters \(before\) $\\to$ Result Execution $\\to$ Result) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 712 Td (  Filters \(after\) $\\to$ Resource Filters \(after\)\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 699 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 683 Td (Q043: Configuration System: `IOptions` vs `IOptionsSnapshot` vs `IOptionsMonitor`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 668 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 655 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 642 Td (* Built on Microsoft.Extensions.Options framework for strongly typed settings.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 629 Td (* **`IOptions<T>`**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 616 Td (* Lifetime: Registered as **Singleton**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 603 Td (* Reads configuration once at startup. Does *not* detect changes if `appsettings.json` is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 592 Td (  modified at runtime. Cannot be recomputed per request.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 579 Td (* **`IOptionsSnapshot<T>`**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 566 Td (* Lifetime: Registered as **Scoped**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 553 Td (* Recomputed once per HTTP request. Detects runtime changes to configuration files) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 542 Td (  dynamically. Safe to use in Scoped services.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 529 Td (* Cannot be injected into Singletons \(causes Captive Dependency\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 516 Td (* **`IOptionsMonitor<T>`**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 503 Td (* Lifetime: Registered as **Singleton**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 490 Td (* Provides real-time notifications when configuration changes via `OnChange` listener.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 479 Td (  Returns the most up-to-date value instantly via `.CurrentValue`. Supports named option) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 468 Td (  instances. Safe to inject into Singletons.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 455 Td (* **The Trap**: Injecting `IOptionsSnapshot<T>` into a Singleton service or background) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 444 Td (  worker. It fails with an `InvalidOperationException` due to scope validation. Use) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 433 Td (  `IOptionsMonitor<T>`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 420 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does `IOptionsMonitor` detect configuration file) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 409 Td (  modifications on disk? *\(Answer: It uses physical file provider file watchers / change) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 398 Td (  tokens \(`IChangeToken`\) registered with the OS file system notification APIs\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 385 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 369 Td (Q044: JWT Architecture, Token Invalidation, and Refresh Token Rotation) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 354 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 341 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 328 Td (* **JWT Structure**: Three Base64Url-encoded segments joined by periods:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 317 Td (  `Header.Payload.Signature`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 304 Td (* **Header**: Algorithm \(`alg`, e.g., RS256, HS256\) and token type \(`typ`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 291 Td (* **Payload**: Standard claims \(`sub`, `iss`, `aud`, `exp`, `iat`\) and custom application) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 280 Td (  claims.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 267 Td (* **Signature**: Hash of header + payload signed using the server's private/secret key:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 256 Td (  `HMACSHA256\(base64Url\(header\) + "." + base64Url\(payload\), secret\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 243 Td (* **Stateless Dilemma**: Because JWTs are self-contained and validated cryptographically) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 232 Td (  without database roundtrips, they cannot be natively revoked before their `exp` timestamp) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 221 Td (  expires.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 208 Td (* **Refresh Token Rotation & Revocation**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 195 Td (* Issue short-lived access tokens \(e.g., 5-15 minutes\) and long-lived refresh tokens \(e.g.,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 184 Td (  7 days\) stored in a database or Redis cache with an `IsRevoked` flag and family) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 173 Td (  identifier.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 160 Td (* When the access token expires, client calls `/refresh` with the refresh token.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 147 Td (* Server verifies the refresh token, revokes it immediately, and issues a brand-new token) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 136 Td (  pair \(Rotation\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 123 Td (* **Token Reuse Detection**: If an already-used or revoked refresh token is presented, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 112 Td (  server assumes token theft, revokes the entire token family, and forces all sessions to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 101 Td (  re-authenticate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 88 Td (* **The Trap**: Storing sensitive data \(passwords, PII, credit card numbers\) in a JWT) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 77 Td (  payload. The payload is Base64 encoded, not encrypted, and can be read by anyone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 64 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What is the difference between symmetric signing \(HS256\) vs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.4 0.4 0.4 rg
