BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (* Directly injecting a Scoped `DbContext` into its constructor causes an immediate Captive) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 769 Td (  Dependency crash or thread-concurrency bugs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 756 Td (* **Correct Implementation Pattern**:) Tj ET
0.96 0.96 0.97 rg 45 602.0 505 141.0 re f
0.82 0.84 0.88 RG 0.5 w 45 602.0 505 141.0 re s
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 734 Td (    public class OrderProcessingWorker : BackgroundService {) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 724.5 Td (        private readonly IServiceScopeFactory _scopeFactory;) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 715.0 Td (        public OrderProcessingWorker\(IServiceScopeFactory scopeFactory\) => _scopeFact) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 705.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 696.0 Td (        protected override async Task ExecuteAsync\(CancellationToken stoppingToken\) {) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 686.5 Td (            while \(!stoppingToken.IsCancellationRequested\) {) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 677.0 Td (                using \(var scope = _scopeFactory.CreateScope\(\)\) {) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 667.5 Td (                    var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<AppDbContext>\(\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 658.0 Td (                    await db.ProcessPendingOrdersAsync\(stoppingToken\);) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 648.5 Td (                }) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 639.0 Td (                await Task.Delay\(TimeSpan.FromSeconds\(30\), stoppingToken\);) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 629.5 Td (            }) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 620.0 Td (        }) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 610.5 Td (    }) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 594.0 Td (* Disposing the scope at the end of each iteration disposes the `DbContext`, clearing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 583.0 Td (  change tracker memory and releasing database connection pool slots.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 570.0 Td (* **The Trap**: Creating a single `IServiceScope` outside the `while` loop. The `DbContext`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 559.0 Td (  remains alive for days, growing out of memory as tracked entities accumulate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 546.0 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What happens if an unhandled exception is thrown inside) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 535.0 Td (  `ExecuteAsync` in .NET 6+? *\(Answer: By default, the host process logs the critical) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 524.0 Td (  failure, aborts execution, and shuts down the entire application process\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 511.0 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 495.0 Td (Q048: Rate Limiting Middleware Architecture \(.NET 7+\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 480.0 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 467.0 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 454.0 Td (* Native rate limiting built into ASP.NET Core via `System.Threading.RateLimiting`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 441.0 Td (* Four Core Algorithms:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 428.0 Td (* **Fixed Window**: Allows $N$ requests per fixed time interval \(e.g., 100 req/min\). Prone) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 417.0 Td (  to boundary traffic spikes \(bursts at the edge of the window\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 404.0 Td (* **Sliding Window**: Divides time into segments, smoothing out fixed window traffic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 393.0 Td (  boundary spikes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 380.0 Td (* **Token Bucket**: Accumulates tokens at a constant refill rate up to a max capacity;) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 369.0 Td (  allows bursts when tokens are available.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 356.0 Td (* **Concurrency Limiter**: Limits active concurrent requests executing simultaneously) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 345.0 Td (  \(e.g., max 50 concurrent requests\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 332.0 Td (* Can be applied globally or per endpoint/group via `.RequireRateLimiting\("PolicyName"\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 321.0 Td (  Returns HTTP 429 Too Many Requests with `Retry-After` headers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 308.0 Td (* **The Trap**: Implementing rate limiting purely in-memory across a multi-instance,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 297.0 Td (  load-balanced web farm without sticky sessions or distributed token storage. Clients can) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 286.0 Td (  bypass limits by hitting different server pods.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 273.0 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How do you implement partitioned rate limiting per client IP or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 262.0 Td (  authenticated tenant? *\(Answer: Use `PartitionedRateLimiter.Create<HttpContext, string>`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 251.0 Td (  to partition buckets dynamically using client IP address or JWT tenant claim\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 238.0 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 222.0 Td (Q049: Global Exception Handling Architecture: `IExceptionHandler` \(.NET 8+\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 207.0 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 194.0 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 181.0 Td (* Legacy approach: Custom middleware \(`try { await next\(\); } catch { ... }`\) or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 170.0 Td (  `app.UseExceptionHandler\(\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 157.0 Td (* **Modern Standard \(.NET 8+\)**: `IExceptionHandler` interface.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 144.0 Td (* **Mechanics**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 131.0 Td (* Implement `IExceptionHandler.TryHandleAsync\(HttpContext, Exception, CancellationToken\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 118.0 Td (* Registered via `builder.Services.AddExceptionHandler<GlobalExceptionHandler>\(\)` and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 107.0 Td (  `app.UseExceptionHandler\(\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 94.0 Td (* Supports chain of responsibility: multiple handlers can be registered. Returns `true` if) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 83.0 Td (  the exception was handled, stopping the chain; returns `false` to pass to the next) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 72.0 Td (  handler.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.4 0.4 0.4 rg
45 25 Td (INFOSYS & ENTERPRISE .NET INTERVIEW PREPARATION GUIDE  |  Page 79) Tj ET
