BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (* Generates standardized RFC 7807 **ProblemDetails** responses \(`application/problem+json`\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 769 Td (  containing status code, title, detail, instance, and trace ID.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 756 Td (* **The Trap**: Logging sensitive customer data, raw SQL statements, or connection strings) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 745 Td (  in the ProblemDetails response returned to external clients. Sensitive technical details) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 734 Td (  belong in internal structured logs only.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 721 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What happens if an exception is thrown *during* the execution of) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 710 Td (  an `IExceptionHandler`? *\(Answer: The exception bubbles up to Kestrel's server-level error) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 699 Td (  handler, which aborts the request and issues a blank HTTP 500\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 686 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 670 Td (Q050: Content Negotiation and Custom Output Formatters) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 655 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 642 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 629 Td (* Content Negotiation \(ConNeg\) selects the best representation for a given response when) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 618 Td (  there are multiple representations available.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 605 Td (* Driven by HTTP headers: `Accept` \(MIME types, e.g., `application/json`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 594 Td (  `application/xml`, `text/csv`\) and `Accept-Language`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 581 Td (* The ASP.NET Core runtime evaluates `OutputFormatters` registered in `MvcOptions`. By) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 570 Td (  default, `SystemTextJsonOutputFormatter` is first.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 557 Td (* If a client requests `Accept: application/xml`, the runtime matches) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 546 Td (  `XmlDataContractSerializerOutputFormatter` if enabled via) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 535 Td (  `AddXmlDataContractSerializerFormatters\(\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 522 Td (* If no matching formatter is found and `ReturnHttpNotAcceptable = true` is configured,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 511 Td (  ASP.NET Core returns HTTP 406 Not Acceptable.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 498 Td (* **The Trap**: Setting `ReturnHttpNotAcceptable = false` \(the default\). If the client) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 487 Td (  requests XML and XML is not configured, ASP.NET Core silently ignores the header and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 476 Td (  returns JSON, violating strict REST API contracts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 463 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How do you implement a custom `CsvOutputFormatter` for high-speed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 452 Td (  reporting? *\(Answer: Inherit from `TextOutputFormatter`, specify supported media types) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 441 Td (  `text/csv`, and override `WriteResponseBodyAsync` using a `StreamWriter` to serialize) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 430 Td (  object properties directly to the response stream\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 417 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 401 Td (Q051: CORS Mechanics: Simple Requests vs Preflight `OPTIONS`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 386 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 373 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 360 Td (* Cross-Origin Resource Sharing \(CORS\) is a **browser security standard**, not a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 349 Td (  server-side firewall. The browser enforces it to prevent unauthorized cross-origin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 338 Td (  requests.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 325 Td (* **Simple Requests**: Meet specific criteria \(GET/POST/HEAD, standard headers like) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 314 Td (  `Accept`, `Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded`, `multipart/form-data`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 303 Td (  `text/plain`\). Browser sends the request immediately with an `Origin` header. Server) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 292 Td (  replies with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 279 Td (* **Preflight Requests \(`OPTIONS`\)**: Triggered when using custom headers \(`Authorization`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 268 Td (  `X-Correlation-Id`\) or complex MIME types \(`application/json`\) or HTTP methods like) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 257 Td (  `PUT`/`DELETE`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 244 Td (* Browser sends an `OPTIONS` request first with `Access-Control-Request-Method` and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 233 Td (  `Access-Control-Request-Headers`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 220 Td (* Server must approve before the browser transmits the actual HTTP request.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 207 Td (* **The Trap**: Placing `app.UseCors\(\)` in the wrong middleware position. In ASP.NET Core,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 196 Td (  `app.UseCors\(\)` **must** be placed after `UseRouting\(\)`, but before `UseAuthentication\(\)`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 185 Td (  and `UseAuthorization\(\)`. If placed after, preflight OPTIONS requests fail with 401/403.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 172 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: Can a malicious hacker bypass CORS using Postman or a console) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 161 Td (  curl script? *\(Answer: Yes, completely. CORS is strictly enforced by web browsers. Backend) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 150 Td (  APIs must use authentication and authorization tokens to secure endpoints\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 137 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 121 Td (Q052: Health Checks Architecture: Liveness vs Readiness Probes in Kubernetes) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 106 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 93 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 80 Td (* Configured using `builder.Services.AddHealthChecks\(\)` and `app.MapHealthChecks\(\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 67 Td (* **Liveness Probe \(`/healthz/live`\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.4 0.4 0.4 rg
