BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (* Answers: "Is the process alive and running?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 767 Td (* Should be lightweight; returns HTTP 200 if the web process is responsive. Should *never*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 756 Td (  check downstream databases or external services.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 743 Td (* If it fails, Kubernetes restarts the pod container.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 730 Td (* **Readiness Probe \(`/healthz/ready`\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 717 Td (* Answers: "Is this instance ready to accept incoming user traffic?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 704 Td (* Validates downstream dependencies: Database connectivity, Redis cache availability,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 693 Td (  message broker health.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 680 Td (* If it fails, Kubernetes removes the pod from the Service load balancer traffic pool) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 669 Td (  without killing or restarting the pod.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 656 Td (* **The Trap**: Checking database connection health in a Liveness probe. If the database) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 645 Td (  goes down for 30 seconds, Kubernetes kills and restarts *all* web pods simultaneously in a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 634 Td (  cascading restart storm, worsening the outage.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 621 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How do you prevent health checks from overwhelming a failing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 610 Td (  database during an incident? *\(Answer: Cache health check results for 10-15 seconds using) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 599 Td (  custom health check caching decorators or response caching\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 586 Td (---) Tj ET
0.7 0.7 0.7 RG 0.5 w 45 558 m 350 558 l S
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.25 rg 45 560 Td (CATEGORY 4: ENTITY FRAMEWORK CORE) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 542 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 526 Td (Q053: `DbContext` Lifecycle, Internal Architecture, and Thread Safety) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 511 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 498 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 485 Td (* `DbContext` represents a combination of the **Unit of Work** and **Repository** design) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 474 Td (  patterns.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 461 Td (* Manages database connections, translates LINQ expressions to SQL queries, caches compiled) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 450 Td (  queries, and tracks changes to entity instances via the `ChangeTracker`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 437 Td (* **Thread-Safety**: `DbContext` is **not** thread-safe. EF Core does not support multiple) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 426 Td (  concurrent operations running on the same context instance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 413 Td (* Calling concurrent queries via `Task.WhenAll\(db.Orders.ToListAsync\(\),) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 402 Td (  db.Users.ToListAsync\(\)\)` on the same `DbContext` instance immediately throws:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 391 Td (  `InvalidOperationException: A second operation was started on this context instance before) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 380 Td (  a previous operation completed`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 367 Td (* **The Trap**: Sharing a single `DbContext` instance across multiple parallel worker tasks) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 356 Td (  or using it in a multi-threaded singleton without creating independent scopes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 343 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does `IDbContextFactory<TContext>` resolve concurrency when) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 332 Td (  processing parallel asynchronous streams? *\(Answer: It creates short-lived, independent) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 321 Td (  `DbContext` instances per parallel task that can be independently consumed and disposed\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 308 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 292 Td (Q054: Change Tracker Mechanics and Entity States) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 277 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 264 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 251 Td (* EF Core tracks changes using `EntityEntry` objects inside the `ChangeTracker`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 238 Td (* Five Core States:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 225 Td (* **Detached**: Entity is not tracked by the context.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 212 Td (* **Unchanged**: Entity is tracked; matches current database state.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 199 Td (* **Added**: Entity is tracked; will be inserted into the database upon `SaveChanges\(\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 186 Td (* **Modified**: Entity is tracked; one or more property values have changed; will be) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 175 Td (  updated via `UPDATE` SQL statement.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 162 Td (* **Deleted**: Entity is tracked; will be deleted via `DELETE` SQL statement upon) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 151 Td (  `SaveChanges\(\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 138 Td (* **Snapshot Tracking vs Notification Tracking**: By default, EF Core creates a snapshot) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 127 Td (  copy of all entity property values when entities are loaded into memory. When) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 116 Td (  `SaveChanges\(\)` is invoked, it runs `DetectChanges\(\)`, comparing the current entity values) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 105 Td (  against the initial snapshot to generate minimal SQL UPDATE statements.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 92 Td (* **The Trap**: Loading thousands of entities into a tracked `DbContext`. Running) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 81 Td (  `DetectChanges\(\)` during `SaveChanges\(\)` traverses every property of every tracked entity,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 70 Td (  causing severe CPU spikes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.4 0.4 0.4 rg
45 25 Td (INFOSYS & ENTERPRISE .NET INTERVIEW PREPARATION GUIDE  |  Page 81) Tj ET
