BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What is `ChangeTracker.Clear\(\)` and when should it be called in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 769 Td (  batch processing? *\(Answer: Clears all tracked entities from memory, resetting the change) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 758 Td (  tracker to avoid memory bloat and prevent cross-entity state pollution during batch) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 747 Td (  loops\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 734 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 718 Td (Q055: `AsNoTracking` vs `AsNoTrackingWithIdentityResolution` Performance) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 703 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 690 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 677 Td (* **`AsNoTracking\(\)`**: Instructs EF Core not to track query results in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 666 Td (  `ChangeTracker`. EF Core skips creating snapshot objects, bypasses `DetectChanges\(\)`, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 655 Td (  saves substantial CPU and memory. Essential for read-only queries.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 642 Td (* **The Identity Resolution Dilemma**: In standard `AsNoTracking\(\)`, if a query returns) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 631 Td (  multiple child records referencing the same parent record \(e.g., Orders containing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 620 Td (  OrderItems referencing the same Product\), EF Core instantiates a *new, duplicate* Product) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 609 Td (  instance in memory for every row.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 596 Td (* **`AsNoTrackingWithIdentityResolution\(\)`**: Does not track entities for changes, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 585 Td (  maintains a temporary lookup table during query execution to ensure that multiple rows) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 574 Td (  with the same primary key share the *same* single entity instance in memory.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 561 Td (* **The Trap**: Using `AsNoTracking\(\)` when updating entities later in the same request) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 550 Td (  without explicitly calling `db.Attach\(\)` or `db.Update\(\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 537 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does configuring `QueryTrackingBehavior.NoTracking` globally) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 526 Td (  at the `DbContext` level affect application design? *\(Answer: Sets read-only behavior as) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 515 Td (  default, requiring developers to explicitly opt-in to tracking via `.AsTracking\(\)` on) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 504 Td (  mutation workflows\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 491 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 475 Td (Q056: The N+1 Query Problem: Detection, Impact, and Fixes) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 460 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Basic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 447 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 434 Td (* Occurs when an application executes 1 initial database query to retrieve $N$ parent) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 423 Td (  records, followed by $N$ individual separate database queries to fetch related child) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 412 Td (  records for each parent.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 399 Td (* **Root Causes**: Lazy loading triggered inside loops, or un-eagerly loaded navigation) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 388 Td (  properties accessed during serialization or view mapping.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 375 Td (* **Impact**: Multiplies database latency by $N$, saturates connection pools, exhausts) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 364 Td (  database CPU, and degrades API response times exponentially.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 351 Td (* **Fixes**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 338 Td (* Eager Loading via `.Include\(\)` and `.ThenInclude\(\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 325 Td (* Projection via `.Select\(x => new DTO { ... }\)` which generates an optimized SQL query) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 314 Td (  fetching only required columns.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 301 Td (* Explicit Batch Loading using `.Load\(\)` or separate joined queries.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 288 Td (* **The Trap**: Enabling lazy loading proxies \(`UseLazyLoadingProxies\(\)`\) in modern Web) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 277 Td (  APIs. Returning an entity with navigation properties from a controller causes JSON) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 266 Td (  serializers to trigger a cascade of hundreds of synchronous SQL queries during) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 255 Td (  serialization.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 242 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How can EF Core be configured to automatically throw an exception) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 231 Td (  when an N+1 query or client-side evaluation occurs? *\(Answer: Configure) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 220 Td (  `optionsBuilder.ConfigureWarnings\(w =>) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 209 Td (  w.Throw\(RelationalEventId.MultipleCollectionIncludeWarning\)\)` or log query execution) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 198 Td (  events\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 185 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 169 Td (Q057: Eager Loading vs Explicit Loading vs Lazy Loading) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 154 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 141 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 128 Td (* **Eager Loading**: Loads related data as part of the initial database query using) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 117 Td (  `.Include\(\)` and `.ThenInclude\(\)`. Translates into SQL `LEFT JOIN` statements \(or split) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 106 Td (  queries\). Best when related data is always needed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 93 Td (* **Explicit Loading**: Loads related data explicitly on-demand at a later time for an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 82 Td (  already-tracked entity using `context.Entry\(parent\).Collection\(p =>) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 71 Td (  p.Children\).LoadAsync\(\)` or `.Reference\(p => p.Child\).LoadAsync\(\)`. Useful when related) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.4 0.4 0.4 rg
