BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 646 Td (Q058: Split Queries \(`AsSplitQuery`\) vs Single Query Performance) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 631 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 618 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 605 Td (* When loading multiple collection navigations via `.Include\(\)` in a single query, EF Core) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 594 Td (  generates a SQL query with multiple `LEFT JOIN` clauses.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 581 Td (* **Cartesian Explosion**: Joining multiple collections creates a Cartesian product where) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 570 Td (  duplicate parent columns are transmitted across the network millions of times, consuming) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 559 Td (  database CPU and network bandwidth.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 546 Td (* **`AsSplitQuery\(\)`**: Instructs EF Core to split the query into multiple separate SQL) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 535 Td (  queries \(one for the parent table, and one for each included collection\) executed over the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 524 Td (  same database connection. EF Core stitches the resulting entities together in memory.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 511 Td (* **Trade-off / Trap**: Split queries do *not* guarantee data consistency if the database) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 500 Td (  is concurrently modified between query executions \(unless wrapped in an explicit) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 489 Td (  serializable or snapshot database transaction\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 476 Td (* **The Trap**: Using `AsSplitQuery\(\)` blindly without transactions on high-frequency) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 465 Td (  update tables, resulting in partial or phantom child entities being stitched to parents.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 452 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How do you configure EF Core to use split queries globally while) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 441 Td (  overriding it for specific atomic queries? *\(Answer: Call `options.UseSqlServer\(conn, o =>) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 430 Td (  o.UseQuerySplittingBehavior\(QuerySplittingBehavior.SplitQuery\)\)` and override locally with) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 419 Td (  `.AsSingleQuery\(\)`\)*.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 406 Td (---) Tj ET
