BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 780 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 764 Td (Q060: Optimistic Concurrency and `DbUpdateConcurrencyException`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 749 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 736 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 723 Td (* In high-throughput systems, pessimistic database locks \(`SELECT FOR UPDATE`\) degrade) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 712 Td (  performance. EF Core implements **Optimistic Concurrency Control**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 699 Td (* Configured using a Concurrency Token column, typically a SQL Server `rowversion` /) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 688 Td (  `byte[]` marked with `[Timestamp]` or `.IsRowVersion\(\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 675 Td (* **Mechanism**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 662 Td (* Entity is read with its current `RowVersion` value \(e.g., `0x0001`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 649 Td (* When `SaveChanges\(\)` executes, EF Core emits an `UPDATE` statement with a `WHERE` clause) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 638 Td (  verifying the token:) Tj ET
0.96 0.96 0.97 rg 45 607.5 505 17.5 re f
0.82 0.84 0.88 RG 0.5 w 45 607.5 505 17.5 re s
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 616 Td (       UPDATE Orders SET Status = 'Shipped' WHERE Id = 101 AND RowVersion = 0x0001;) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 599.5 Td (* The database returns the number of affected rows. If another transaction modified the row) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 588.5 Td (  in the interim, `RowVersion` changed; affected rows is $0$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 575.5 Td (* EF Core detects 0 affected rows and throws `DbUpdateConcurrencyException`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 562.5 Td (* **The Trap**: Catching `DbUpdateConcurrencyException` and doing nothing. You must resolve) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 551.5 Td (  the conflict: reload the database values via `entry.GetDatabaseValuesAsync\(\)`, apply merge) Tj ET
