BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (* When complex SQL reporting queries exceed LINQ translation capabilities, raw SQL is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 769 Td (  required.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 756 Td (* **`FromSqlInterpolated`**: **Safe against SQL Injection**. Uses C# string interpolation) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 745 Td (  syntax \(`$"SELECT * FROM Orders WHERE CustomerId = {customerId}"`\), but EF Core intercepts) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 734 Td (  the interpolated string and converts variables into parameterized `DbParameter` SQL) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 723 Td (  arguments \(`@p0`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 710 Td (* **`FromSqlRaw`**: Accepts a format string and parameters array. If a developer uses raw) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 699 Td (  string concatenation \(`"SELECT * FROM Orders WHERE CustomerId = " + customerId`\), the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 688 Td (  query is vulnerable to catastrophic **SQL Injection**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 675 Td (* **Composability**: Raw SQL queries can be composed with LINQ operators \(`.Where\(\)`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 664 Td (  `.OrderBy\(\)`, `.Take\(\)`\) provided the raw SQL does not contain stored procedure executions) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 653 Td (  or CTEs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 640 Td (* **The Trap**: Passing user-supplied strings directly into `FromSqlRaw` using) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 629 Td (  `string.Format` or string concatenation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 616 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What requirements must be met for a raw SQL query to return) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 605 Td (  entities via `FromSqlInterpolated`? *\(Answer: Must return all columns mapped by the entity) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 594 Td (  type, column names must match entity property names, and the query cannot contain joins to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 583 Td (  other tables unless projected into an unmapped keyless type\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 570 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 554 Td (Q066: Compiled Queries \(`EF.CompileAsyncQuery`\) Mechanics) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 539 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 526 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 513 Td (* Normal LINQ query execution pipeline:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 500 Td (* Parse LINQ expression tree.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 487 Td (* Check compiled query cache.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 474 Td (* Generate relational SQL command AST.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 461 Td (* Format SQL string and parameters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 448 Td (* Execute against database.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 435 Td (* Step 1-4 incur CPU overhead. Although EF Core caches query plans internally, expression) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 424 Td (  tree hashing still incurs CPU cycles.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 411 Td (* **`EF.CompileAsyncQuery`**: Compiles the LINQ query directly into an invokable delegate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 400 Td (  once and stores it in a `static readonly` field.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 387 Td (* Completely bypasses LINQ expression tree compilation on subsequent calls, delivering) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 376 Td (  near-raw-ADO.NET execution performance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 363 Td (* **The Trap**: Using compiled queries for dynamic queries with changing `Where`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 352 Td (  conditions. Compiled queries require fixed query structures with varying parameters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 339 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: Why did compiled queries become less critical in EF Core 6/7/8?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 328 Td (  *\(Answer: The internal query compilation pipeline was heavily optimized with fast) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 317 Td (  pre-computed hashes and source-generated query plans, making manual compiled queries) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 306 Td (  necessary only for extreme micro-benchmarks\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 293 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 277 Td (Q067: EF Core Interceptors vs `SaveChanges` Overrides) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 262 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 249 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 236 Td (* **`SaveChanges` Overrides**: Traditional approach. Override `SaveChangesAsync` in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 225 Td (  `DbContext` to iterate through `ChangeTracker.Entries\(\)`, automatically populating) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 214 Td (  `CreatedDate`, `UpdatedDate`, or emitting domain events.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 201 Td (* **Interceptors** \(Introduced in EF Core 3+ / 7+\): Decouple cross-cutting database) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 190 Td (  operations from the `DbContext` class.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 177 Td (* Types of Interceptors:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 164 Td (* **`ISaveChangesInterceptor`**: Intercepts `SavingChanges` and `SavedChanges`. Ideal for) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 153 Td (  domain event dispatching and auditing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 140 Td (* **`IDbCommandInterceptor`**: Intercepts low-level SQL command creation, execution, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 129 Td (  failure. Ideal for custom SQL tagging, query logging, and fault injection.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 116 Td (* **`IDbConnectionInterceptor`**: Intercepts connection opening/closing \(e.g., fetching) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 105 Td (  dynamic Azure Active Directory access tokens before opening a connection\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 92 Td (* **The Trap**: Modifying the Change Tracker inside an async `SavedChanges` interceptor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 81 Td (  Changes made after database persistence has completed will not be written to the database) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 70 Td (  unless `SaveChanges` is called again, risking infinite loops.) Tj ET
