BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (* Scans the outer table and performs a lookup \(typically index seek\) into the inner table) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 769 Td (  for every outer row.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 756 Td (* Optimal for: Small outer table and indexed inner table. Highly efficient for OLTP.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 743 Td (* **Merge Join**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 730 Td (* Requires **both** inputs to be pre-sorted on the join key. Reads both streams) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 719 Td (  simultaneously in a single pass \($O\(N + M\)$\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 706 Td (* Optimal for: Medium-to-large sorted datasets. Very low CPU and memory overhead; does not) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 695 Td (  require memory grants.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 682 Td (* **Hash Match Join**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 669 Td (* Builds an in-memory hash table from the smaller input \(build input\), then scans the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 658 Td (  larger input \(probe input\) looking up matching hash keys.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 645 Td (* Optimal for: Large, unsorted, un-indexed datasets \(typical in OLAP/data warehousing\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 632 Td (* Trade-off: Requires substantial **Memory Grants**. If the hash table exceeds allocated) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 621 Td (  memory, it spills to `tempdb` \(Hash Spill\), causing severe disk I/O latency.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 608 Td (* **The Trap**: Assuming Hash Match is always better because it handles large tables. In) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 597 Td (  OLTP systems, unexpected Hash Joins usually indicate missing indexes or poor cardinality) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 586 Td (  estimates resulting from stale statistics.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 573 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What causes a Nested Loops Join to degrade into terrible) Tj ET
