BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 355.5 Td (Q074: Parameter Sniffing: Mechanics, Diagnosis, and Remediation) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 340.5 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 327.5 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 314.5 Td (* When a parameterized query or stored procedure is executed for the first time, SQL Server) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 303.5 Td (  **sniffs** the parameter values passed and generates an execution plan tailored) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 292.5 Td (  specifically to the cardinality of those specific inputs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 279.5 Td (* The plan is stored in the plan cache for subsequent executions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 266.5 Td (* **The Problem**: If the procedure is first compiled with an atypical parameter \(e.g., a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 255.5 Td (  customer with 5 orders $\\to$ generates an Index Seek + Key Lookup\), and later executed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 244.5 Td (  with an enterprise customer having 5,000,000 orders, the cached plan performs 5,000,000) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 233.5 Td (  Key Lookups, causing extreme CPU spikes and timeout errors.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 220.5 Td (* **Remediation Techniques**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 207.5 Td (* **`OPTIMIZE FOR \(@Param = value\)`**: Compiles the plan for a typical average value.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 194.5 Td (* **`OPTIMIZE FOR UNKNOWN`**: Uses statistical average densities instead of sniffing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 183.5 Td (  specific values.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 170.5 Td (* **`WITH RECOMPILE`**: Forces plan recompilation on every execution \(best for volatile,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 159.5 Td (  infrequently run batch reports\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 146.5 Td (* **Local Variable Trick**: Copy parameter to local variable inside the procedure \(`DECLARE) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 135.5 Td (  @LocalVar INT = @Param`\). SQL Server disables parameter sniffing for local variables and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 124.5 Td (  uses average density.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 111.5 Td (* **The Trap**: Blindly slapping `WITH RECOMPILE` on every procedure. In high-throughput) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 100.5 Td (  OLTP systems handling 5,000 requests/second, recompiling on every call exhausts CPU) Tj ET
