BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 677 Td (  error.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 664 Td (* **Consistency**: Database transitions from one valid state to another valid state,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 653 Td (  preserving all schema constraints, foreign keys, unique keys, and check rules.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 640 Td (* **Isolation**: Concurrent transactions execute without interfering with one another.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 629 Td (  Dictated by Transaction Isolation Levels.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 616 Td (* **Durability**: Once a transaction is committed, its changes survive system crashes or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 605 Td (  power failures. Achieved by flushing log records to non-volatile disk before acknowledging) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 594 Td (  commit to client.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 581 Td (* **The Trap**: Believing "Consistency" in ACID is the same as "Consistency" in the CAP) Tj ET
