BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 701 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 688 Td (* **CTE \(Common Table Expression\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 675 Td (* Non-materialized query syntax sugar. Exists only for the duration of a single statement.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 662 Td (* Evaluated in-line with the outer query. Supports recursion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 649 Td (* **Temp Table \(`#Temp`\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 636 Td (* Physical table created in `tempdb`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 623 Td (* Fully supports statistics, parallel query execution, column indexes, and constraints.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 610 Td (* Can be modified with `UPDATE`/`DELETE`. Scope: current session/procedure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 597 Td (* Best for: Large intermediate datasets \($> 1,000$ rows\) reused across multiple queries.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 584 Td (* **Table Variable \(`@Table`\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 571 Td (* Memory/`tempdb` construct scoped to current batch.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 558 Td (* Historically does **not** maintain statistics \(compiler assumed cardinality was always 1) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 547 Td (  row, causing terrible plans on large datasets; improved in SQL Server 2019 Deferred) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 536 Td (  Compilation\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 523 Td (* Does not participate in transactions/rollbacks \(`ROLLBACK` does not revert changes\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 510 Td (* Best for: Very small datasets \($< 100$ rows\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 497 Td (* **The Trap**: Using Table Variables for large datasets expecting them to "live purely in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 486 Td (  RAM". Table variables write to `tempdb` just like temp tables when data exceeds small page) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 475 Td (  thresholds, but lack statistics.) Tj ET
