BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 396 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 383 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 370 Td (* **Partitioning**: Divides a large table physically into smaller independent chunks) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 359 Td (  \(partitions\) across filegroups based on a **Partition Key** \(typically date\), while) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 348 Td (  remaining a single logical table.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 335 Td (* **Components**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 322 Td (* **Partition Function**: Maps boundary values \(`RANGE RIGHT` or `RANGE LEFT`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 309 Td (* **Partition Scheme**: Maps partitions to physical Filegroups/Disks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 296 Td (* **Partition Elimination \(Pruning\)**: When a query includes the partition key in its) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 285 Td (  `WHERE` clause, the engine scans *only* the matching partition, ignoring gigabytes of) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 274 Td (  irrelevant data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 261 Td (* **Sliding Window Pattern**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 248 Td (* Enterprise data archival pattern for rolling logs/audit tables.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 235 Td (* Archive old data and load new data near-instantly in $O\(1\)$ time via metadata-only) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 224 Td (  operations: `ALTER TABLE ... SWITCH PARTITION` without running slow `DELETE` or `INSERT`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 213 Td (  transactions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 200 Td (* **The Trap**: Creating non-aligned indexes on a partitioned table. For `SWITCH PARTITION`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 189 Td (  to execute instantly, all clustered and non-clustered indexes must be aligned to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 178 Td (  identical partition scheme.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 165 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What is the performance difference between deleting 10 million) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 154 Td (  rows via `DELETE FROM Logs WHERE Date < '2025-01-01'` vs switching a partition? *\(Answer:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 143 Td (  `DELETE` logs millions of row deletions in transaction log taking hours and locking the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 132 Td (  table; `SWITCH PARTITION` changes metadata pointers in milliseconds with zero transaction) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 121 Td (  log bloat\).*) Tj ET
