BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (* The SQL Server Transaction Log \(`.ldf`\) operates on a circular ring buffer divided into) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 769 Td (  smaller segments called **Virtual Log Files \(VLFs\)**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 756 Td (* Implements **Write-Ahead Logging \(WAL\)**: Data modifications are written to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 745 Td (  transaction log buffer and hardened to disk *before* the dirty data pages in the buffer) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 734 Td (  pool are written to the data file \(`.mdf`\) by the Checkpoint process.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 721 Td (* **Log Truncation**: Frees inactive VLFs for reuse. In Simple Recovery Model, truncation) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 710 Td (  occurs at Checkpoint. In Full Recovery Model, truncation occurs **only** after a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 699 Td (  successful Transaction Log Backup.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 686 Td (* **The High VLF Trap**: If a log file grows in frequent, tiny increments \(e.g., autogrow) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 675 Td (  by 1MB\), SQL Server creates tens of thousands of tiny VLFs. High VLF count \($> 10,000$\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 664 Td (  slows down database startup, crash recovery, replication, and log backups.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 651 Td (* **The Trap**: Assuming `SHRINKFILE` fixes log growth. Shrinking a log file fragments VLFs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 640 Td (  and causes immediate auto-growth cycles. You must fix the root cause \(e.g., unscheduled) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 629 Td (  log backups or uncommitted transactions\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 616 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What does `log_reuse_wait_desc` in `sys.databases` reveal?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 605 Td (  *\(Answer: Explains why the transaction log cannot be truncated, such as `LOG_BACKUP`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 594 Td (  `ACTIVE_TRANSACTION`, `REPLICATION`, or `CHECKPOINT`\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 581 Td (---) Tj ET
0.7 0.7 0.7 RG 0.5 w 45 553 m 350 553 l S
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.25 rg 45 555 Td (CATEGORY 6: OOP & DESIGN PATTERNS) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 537 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 521 Td (Q085: Encapsulation vs Information Hiding) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 506 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 493 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 480 Td (* **Encapsulation**: The bundling of data \(fields\) and the behaviors \(methods\) that operate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 469 Td (  on that data into a cohesive unit \(class\), while protecting object state invariants.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 456 Td (* **Information Hiding**: The principle of concealing internal structural and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 445 Td (  implementation decisions behind a stable public contract/interface. Clients depend on) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 434 Td (  *what* a component does, not *how* it stores or computes it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 421 Td (* **The Anemic Domain Model Trap**: Creating entities with public getters and setters for) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 410 Td (  all properties \(`public decimal Balance { get; set; }`\). This encapsulates data into a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 399 Td (  class, but provides **zero information hiding or invariant protection**. External services) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 388 Td (  can set `Balance = -9999` bypassing business logic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 375 Td (* **Rich Domain Model**: Private setters, mutated only via domain methods \(`Debit\(decimal) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 364 Td (  amount\)`\), enforcing validation and invariants internally.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 351 Td (* **The Trap**: Claiming properties with `{ get; set; }` provide encapsulation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 340 Td (  Auto-properties with public setters are syntactically identical to public fields in terms) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 329 Td (  of invariant safety.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 316 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does Domain-Driven Design \(DDD\) enforce encapsulation within) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 305 Td (  Aggregate Roots? *\(Answer: Entities within an aggregate cannot be referenced or mutated) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 294 Td (  directly from outside; all mutations must flow through methods on the Aggregate Root\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 281 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 265 Td (Q086: Interface vs Abstract Class Decision Matrix) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 250 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Basic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 237 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 224 Td (* **Interface**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 211 Td (* Defines a contract of *what* capabilities an implementer must provide.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 198 Td (* Supports multiple inheritance: a class can implement dozens of interfaces.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 185 Td (* Represents an **"IS-CAN-DO"** relationship \(e.g., `IDisposable`, `IComparable`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 174 Td (  `IOrderValidator`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 161 Td (* Contains no instance fields/state \(prior to C# 8, no method implementations; C# 8) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 150 Td (  introduced Default Interface Methods, but these cannot hold instance state\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 137 Td (* **Abstract Class**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 124 Td (* Serves as an incomplete base class providing common shared behavior, state, and template) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 113 Td (  algorithms.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 100 Td (* Single inheritance: a class can inherit from only one base class.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 87 Td (* Represents an **"IS-A"** relationship \(e.g., `PaymentGatewayBase`, `EntityBase`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 74 Td (* Can have constructors, instance fields, state, and access modifiers \(`protected`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 63 Td (  `internal`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.4 0.4 0.4 rg
