BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (* **The Trap**: Using an abstract class when an interface was required because you wanted) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 769 Td (  to share 3 lines of utility code, locking derived classes into a rigid single-inheritance) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 758 Td (  hierarchy.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 745 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What is the purpose of Default Interface Methods \(DIM\) in modern) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 734 Td (  C#? *\(Answer: Allows library authors to evolve an interface by adding new methods with) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 723 Td (  default implementations without breaking existing third-party implementers\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 710 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 694 Td (Q087: Liskov Substitution Principle \(LSP\) Violations in Enterprise Code) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 679 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 666 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 653 Td (* **LSP Formulation**: Subtypes must be substitutable for their base types without altering) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 642 Td (  the correctness of the program.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 629 Td (* **Enterprise Violation Smells**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 616 Td (* **Throwing `NotImplementedException`**: Inheriting from a base class or interface and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 605 Td (  throwing `NotImplementedException` because the derived class does not support that) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 594 Td (  operation \(violates ISP and LSP\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 581 Td (* **Downcasting / Type Checking**: Writing `if \(account is PremiumAccount\)` inside a method) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 570 Td (  that accepts the base `Account`. If you must check concrete types, polymorphism has) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 559 Td (  failed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 546 Td (* **Weakening Postconditions**: Derived class returns `null` or a restricted value where) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 535 Td (  the base contract guaranteed a valid object.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 522 Td (* **Strengthening Preconditions**: Derived class requires stricter validation parameters) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 511 Td (  than the base class contract.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 498 Td (* **The Trap**: The classic "Square inherits from Rectangle" academic trap. If `Rectangle`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 487 Td (  has `SetWidth` and `SetHeight`, changing `Square.SetWidth` unexpectedly mutates height,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 476 Td (  breaking calling code that assumes independent dimensions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 463 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does Refactoring to Interfaces or Composition solve LSP) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 452 Td (  violations caused by forced inheritance hierarchies? *\(Answer: Split fat base classes into) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 441 Td (  granular interfaces; compose components rather than forcing unnatural inheritance) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 430 Td (  relationships\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 417 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 401 Td (Q088: Interface Segregation Principle \(ISP\) and Fat Interfaces) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 386 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 373 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 360 Td (* **ISP Formulation**: Clients should not be forced to depend upon interfaces that they do) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 349 Td (  not use.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 336 Td (* **The Fat Interface Anti-Pattern**: An interface like `IOrderService` containing 40) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 325 Td (  methods \(`CreateOrder`, `CancelOrder`, `GenerateInvoicePdf`, `SendTrackingEmail`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 314 Td (  `ProcessRefund`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 301 Td (* A client that only needs to create an order depends on code that sends emails and prints) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 290 Td (  PDFs. Testing requires mocking 40 methods!) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 277 Td (* **Refactoring Strategy**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 264 Td (* Decompose into focused, role-based interfaces: `IOrderCreator`, `IOrderCancellation`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 253 Td (  `IInvoiceGenerator`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 240 Td (* Alternatively, adopt the **CQRS \(Command Query Responsibility Segregation\)** pattern:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 229 Td (  every use case is an isolated request handler \(`IRequestHandler<CreateOrderCommand,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 218 Td (  OrderResult>`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 205 Td (* **The Trap**: Creating thousands of single-method interfaces blindly for every small) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 194 Td (  operation where no independent client diversity exists. Apply ISP when distinct clients) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 183 Td (  consume distinct subsets of behavior.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 170 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does ISP benefit Unit Testing? *\(Answer: Test fixtures only) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 159 Td (  mock the 1 or 2 methods strictly required for the test scenario, eliminating bloated mock) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 148 Td (  setups\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 135 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 119 Td (Q089: Dependency Inversion Principle \(DIP\) vs Inversion of Control \(IoC\) vs DI) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 104 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Basic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 91 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 78 Td (* **DIP \(Principle\)**: High-level modules should not depend on low-level modules; both) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 67 Td (  should depend on abstractions. Abstractions should not depend on details; details should) Tj ET
