BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (  depend on abstractions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 767 Td (* **IoC \(Architectural Pattern\)**: Inverting the control flow of a program. Instead of user) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 756 Td (  code driving execution and calling framework components, the framework calls user code) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 745 Td (  \(the "Hollywood Principle": *Don't call us, we'll call you*\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 732 Td (* **DI \(Implementation Technique\)**: A specific design pattern used to implement IoC.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 721 Td (  Dependencies are supplied \(injected\) to an object from the outside \(Constructor Injection,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 710 Td (  Property Injection, Method Injection\) rather than the object instantiating them directly) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 699 Td (  via `new`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 686 Td (* Relationship Hierarchy: **DIP** is the overarching architectural goal $\\to$ implemented) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 675 Td (  via **IoC** $\\to$ realized concretely via **Dependency Injection containers**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 662 Td (* **The Trap**: Equating DI with an IoC Container. DI is a design pattern that can be done) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 651 Td (  purely manually \("Pure DI" / "Poor Man's DI"\). An IoC container \(`IServiceProvider`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 640 Td (  Autofac\) is an automated framework tool.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 627 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: Why is the Service Locator pattern considered an anti-pattern) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 616 Td (  compared to Constructor Injection? *\(Answer: Service Locator hides dependencies within) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 605 Td (  class implementations, breaking compile-time safety and API readability, whereas) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 594 Td (  Constructor Injection explicitly declares required contracts\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 581 Td (---) Tj ET
