BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (* **Factory Method**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 767 Td (* Defines an interface or abstract method for creating a single object, allowing subclasses) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 756 Td (  to decide which concrete class to instantiate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 743 Td (* Example: `PaymentProcessorFactory.CreateProcessor\(PaymentType type\) ->) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 732 Td (  IPaymentProcessor`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 719 Td (* **Abstract Factory**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 706 Td (* Provides an interface for creating families of related or dependent objects without) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 695 Td (  specifying their concrete classes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 682 Td (* Example: Cloud Infrastructure Factory `ICloudStorageFactory` producing both) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 671 Td (  `IBlobStorage` and `IQueueStorage` \(Azure implementation produces `AzureBlob` +) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 660 Td (  `AzureQueue`; AWS implementation produces `S3` + `SQS`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 647 Td (* **Enterprise Context**: Used extensively in multi-tenant or multi-region microservices) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 636 Td (  where underlying cloud infrastructure or compliance providers vary based on configuration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 623 Td (* **The Trap**: Creating complex Abstract Factories for single standalone objects where a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 612 Td (  simple `Func<T>` or DI keyed service would suffice.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 599 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How did .NET 8 Keyed Services \(`builder.Services.AddKeyedScoped`\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 588 Td (  modernize the Factory pattern in ASP.NET Core? *\(Answer: Allows registering multiple) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 577 Td (  implementations of the same interface with distinct keys and resolving them directly via) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 566 Td (  `[FromKeyedServices\("stripe"\)] IPaymentProcessor`, reducing the need for custom factory) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 555 Td (  classes\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 542 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 526 Td (Q092: Builder Pattern vs Telescoping Constructor) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 511 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 498 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 485 Td (* **Telescoping Constructor Problem**: Creating overloaded constructors with 1, 2, 3, 4,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 474 Td (  5... parameters \(`Order\(id\)`, `Order\(id, customer\)`, `Order\(id, customer, items\)`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 463 Td (  Inflexible, unreadable, error-prone when multiple parameters share identical types \(e.g.,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 452 Td (  three `string` or `int` parameters\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 439 Td (* **Builder Pattern**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 426 Td (* Separates the construction of a complex object from its representation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 413 Td (* Provides a fluent, readable API with method chaining) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 402 Td (  \(`builder.WithCustomer\(...\).WithItems\(...\).ApplyDiscount\(...\).Build\(\)`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 389 Td (* Enforces step-by-step invariant validation during `Build\(\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 376 Td (* **Enterprise Usage**: Ubiquitous in .NET configuration: `WebApplicationBuilder`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 365 Td (  `IHostBuilder`, `DbContextOptionsBuilder`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 352 Td (* **The Trap**: Allowing the builder to return a partially constructed, invalid domain) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 341 Td (  entity. The `Build\(\)` method must be the gatekeeper that runs complete business validation) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 330 Td (  before returning the immutable object.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 317 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does C# 9+ `init` accessor and record types reduce the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 306 Td (  necessity of manual Builder classes for simple DTOs? *\(Answer: Allows object initializer) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 295 Td (  syntax `new OrderDto { CustomerId = 1 }` while maintaining compile-time immutability after) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 284 Td (  construction\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 271 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 255 Td (Q093: Strategy Pattern vs Switch Statement / Polymorphic Refactoring) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 240 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Basic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 227 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 214 Td (* **The Problem**: A 200-line `switch\(paymentMethod\)` statement in an enterprise checkout) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 203 Td (  service. Violates the **Open/Closed Principle \(OCP\)**: adding a new payment gateway) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 192 Td (  requires editing, re-testing, and redeploying the core checkout service.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 179 Td (* **Strategy Pattern**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 166 Td (* Defines a family of interchangeable algorithms wrapped in an interface) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 155 Td (  \(`IPaymentStrategy`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 142 Td (* Concrete strategies: `CreditCardPaymentStrategy`, `PayPalPaymentStrategy`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 131 Td (  `CryptoPaymentStrategy`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 118 Td (* Context class delegates execution: `_strategy.ProcessPayment\(order\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 105 Td (* New payment methods are added by creating a new class implementing the interface, leaving) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 94 Td (  existing code completely untouched.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 81 Td (* **DI Integration**: Register all strategies in DI as `IEnumerable<IPaymentStrategy>` and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 70 Td (  resolve dynamically using a dictionary keyed by enum/string.) Tj ET
