BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 444.5 Td (  Decorator pattern? *\(Answer: MediatR pipeline behaviors \(`IPipelineBehavior<TRequest,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 433.5 Td (  TResponse>`\) implement the Decorator pattern around MediatR request handlers\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 420.5 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 404.5 Td (Q095: Observer Pattern vs Publish-Subscribe Architecture) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 389.5 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 376.5 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 363.5 Td (* **Observer Pattern**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 350.5 Td (* Implemented within a **single process / memory space**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 337.5 Td (* The Subject maintains a list of Observers \(e.g., C# delegates/events, `IObservable<T>` /) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 326.5 Td (  `IObserver<T>`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 313.5 Td (* Communication is typically direct, synchronous, and tightly coupled in terms of lifecycle) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 302.5 Td (  \(if subject crashes or hangs, observers block\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 289.5 Td (* **Publish-Subscribe \(Pub/Sub\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 276.5 Td (* Distributed architectural pattern operating across **multiple isolated processes or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 265.5 Td (  microservices**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 252.5 Td (* Publishers and Subscribers have **zero direct knowledge** of each other.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 239.5 Td (* Decoupled via an intermediate **Message Broker** \(RabbitMQ, Kafka, Azure Service Bus\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 226.5 Td (* Asynchronous, resilient: if subscribers are offline, messages persist in queues until) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 215.5 Td (  consumed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 202.5 Td (* **The Trap**: Describing event-driven microservices using the term "Observer Pattern".) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 191.5 Td (  Single-process memory events cannot survive process crashes or scale out across servers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 178.5 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What role does Reactive Extensions \(Rx.NET\) play in the Observer) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 167.5 Td (  pattern? *\(Answer: Provides LINQ-style composable queries over asynchronous event streams) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 156.5 Td (  using `IObservable<T>`\)*.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 143.5 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 127.5 Td (Q096: The Repository & Unit of Work Debate with EF Core) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 112.5 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 99.5 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 86.5 Td (* **The Debate**: Should you build a custom `IRepository<T>` and `IUnitOfWork` on top of EF) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 75.5 Td (  Core?) Tj ET
