BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (* **Argument Against \(Redundant Abstraction\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 767 Td (* EF Core's `DbSet<T>` is **already** an implementation of the Repository pattern.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 754 Td (* EF Core's `DbContext` is **already** an implementation of the Unit of Work pattern) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 743 Td (  \(`ChangeTracker` collects mutations, `SaveChangesAsync\(\)` commits atomically\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 730 Td (* Wrapping them in a generic `IRepository<T>` \(`GetById`, `Add`, `Delete`\) strips away EF) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 719 Td (  Core's powerful features \(IQueryable, Include, AsSplitQuery, projection, ExecuteUpdate\) or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 708 Td (  forces developers to expose `IQueryable`, defeating the encapsulation of the repository.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 695 Td (* **Argument For \(Enterprise Pragmatism\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 682 Td (* Restricts junior developers from writing un-indexed, disastrous LINQ queries directly in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 671 Td (  API controllers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 658 Td (* Encapsulates complex aggregate retrieval in Domain-Driven Design \(DDD\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 645 Td (* Enables easy in-memory mocking in unit tests without in-memory database quirks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 632 Td (* **Architectural Consensus**: Avoid *Generic* Repositories \(`IRepository<T>`\). Use) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 621 Td (  *Specific* Repositories \(`IOrderRepository`\) tailored to domain aggregate roots,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 610 Td (  containing explicit business query methods \(`GetPendingApprovalOrdersAsync`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 597 Td (* **The Trap**: Exposing `IQueryable<T>` from a custom repository. This leaks database) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 586 Td (  query translation concerns directly into the presentation layer, completely defeating the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 575 Td (  purpose of the abstraction.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 562 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: Why is EF Core In-Memory Database provider considered an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 551 Td (  anti-pattern for testing repositories? *\(Answer: It behaves differently from relational) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 540 Td (  databases: does not enforce referential integrity, supports operations SQL Server doesn't,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 529 Td (  and hides SQL translation errors. Use Testcontainers with real Docker database instances) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 518 Td (  instead\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 505 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 489 Td (Q097: Chain of Responsibility Pattern in Enterprise Architectures) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 474 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 461 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 448 Td (* Decouples the sender of a request from its receivers by giving multiple objects a chance) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 437 Td (  to handle the request.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 424 Td (* Handlers are linked in a chain. Each handler inspects the request and decides either to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 413 Td (  process it, pass it to the `next` handler in the chain, or short-circuit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 400 Td (* **Ubiquitous Implementations in .NET**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 387 Td (* ASP.NET Core Middleware Pipeline \(`RequestDelegate next`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 374 Td (* MediatR Pipeline Behaviors \(`IPipelineBehavior`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 361 Td (* Validation Pipelines \(e.g., executing FluentValidation rules sequentially before reaching) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 350 Td (  domain handlers\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 337 Td (* Approval Workflows \(e.g., Manager $\\to$ Director $\\to$ VP expense approval\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 324 Td (* **The Trap**: Failing to define a terminal condition or failing to handle cases where no) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 313 Td (  handler in the chain processes the request, leaving requests dropped silently.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 300 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does Chain of Responsibility differ from the Decorator) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 289 Td (  pattern? *\(Answer: Decorator wraps an object to augment its behavior without breaking the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 278 Td (  call; Chain of Responsibility can terminate execution at any link and handlers operate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 267 Td (  independently\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 254 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 238 Td (Q098: Adapter Pattern vs Facade Pattern) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 223 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Basic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 210 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 197 Td (* **Adapter Pattern**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 184 Td (* Converts the interface of an existing class into another interface clients expect.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 171 Td (* Solves **incompatible interfaces** \("Make square peg fit in round hole"\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 158 Td (* Example: Adapting a legacy 3rd-party XML SOAP banking service into your modern REST) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 147 Td (  application's `IPaymentGateway` interface.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 134 Td (* **Facade Pattern**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 121 Td (* Provides a simplified, high-level interface to a complex subsystem or group of classes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 108 Td (* Does *not* reconcile incompatible interfaces; it simplifies complex interaction) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 97 Td (  workflows.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 84 Td (* Example: An `OrderCheckoutFacade` that coordinates inventory deduction, credit card) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 73 Td (  charging, shipping label generation, and confirmation email sending behind a single) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.4 0.4 0.4 rg
45 25 Td (INFOSYS & ENTERPRISE .NET INTERVIEW PREPARATION GUIDE  |  Page 99) Tj ET
