BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (  `PlaceOrder\(\)` method.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 767 Td (* **The Trap**: Confusing their intents: Adapter changes an existing interface to match) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 756 Td (  another; Facade creates a brand-new simpler interface over many existing components.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 743 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: Can an Adapter wrap multiple classes? *\(Answer: Rarely; if it) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 732 Td (  wraps many classes to simplify interaction, it is acting as a Facade. An Adapter strictly) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 721 Td (  focuses on interface reconciliation\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 708 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 692 Td (Q099: Template Method Pattern vs Strategy Pattern) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 677 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 664 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 651 Td (* Both patterns define algorithms and allow variations, but differ in mechanism:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 638 Td (* **Template Method Pattern**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 625 Td (* Relies on **Inheritance**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 612 Td (* The base class defines the invariant skeletal framework of an algorithm in a non-virtual) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 601 Td (  method, with placeholder abstract or virtual steps \(`Hook\(\)` methods\) overridden by) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 590 Td (  subclasses.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 577 Td (* Compile-time bound; rigid hierarchy.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 564 Td (* **Strategy Pattern**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 551 Td (* Relies on **Composition**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 538 Td (* The algorithm is encapsulated within an independent interface. The consuming class holds) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 527 Td (  a reference to the interface and delegates execution.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 514 Td (* Runtime swappable, highly flexible, adheres to the Open/Closed Principle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 501 Td (* **The Trap**: Choosing Template Method over Strategy because "it's quick to inherit".) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 490 Td (  Subclasses become tightly coupled to base class execution ordering, causing breaking) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 479 Td (  changes when base algorithms evolve.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 466 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does ASP.NET Core's `AuthenticationHandler<TOptions>` use the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 455 Td (  Template Method pattern? *\(Answer: The base class manages the authentication plumbing and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 444 Td (  options initialization, invoking the abstract `HandleAuthenticateAsync\(\)` method) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 433 Td (  implemented by concrete schemes like JWT or Cookie\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 420 Td (---) Tj ET
0.7 0.7 0.7 RG 0.5 w 45 392 m 350 392 l S
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.25 rg 45 394 Td (CATEGORY 7: MICROSERVICES & DISTRIBUTED SYSTEMS) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 376 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 360 Td (Q100: Monolith to Microservices Trade-offs and the "Distributed Tax") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 345 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 332 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 319 Td (* Microservices solve organizational scaling problems \(multiple autonomous teams deploying) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 308 Td (  independently\), not raw performance or simplicity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 295 Td (* **The Distributed Tax \(Trade-offs\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 282 Td (* **Network Latency & Unreliability**: In-process method calls \($< 10$ nanoseconds\) become) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 271 Td (  network RPC calls \(5-50 milliseconds\), introducing transient network failures.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 258 Td (* **Dual Writes & Eventual Consistency**: Loss of ACID database transactions; replacing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 247 Td (  atomic commits with distributed Sagas, Outbox patterns, and eventual consistency.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 234 Td (* **Operational Complexity**: Requires Kubernetes, container orchestration, service meshes,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 223 Td (  distributed tracing, centralized logging, and sophisticated CI/CD pipelines.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 210 Td (* **Data Duplication**: Independent databases per service necessitate data replication and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 199 Td (  cache synchronization.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 186 Td (* **Migration Heuristic**: Start with a well-structured **Modular Monolith**. Extract) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 175 Td (  bounded contexts into microservices only when independent deployment cadences, distinct) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 164 Td (  scaling bottlenecks, or strict team ownership boundaries demand it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 151 Td (* **The Trap**: Claiming microservices make applications faster. The network latency and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 140 Td (  serialization overhead makes microservices inherently slower per request than a monolithic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 129 Td (  in-process call.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 116 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does a Modular Monolith enforce architectural boundaries) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 105 Td (  without physical process isolation? *\(Answer: Using C# internal access modifiers,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 94 Td (  independent projects/assemblies per module, architecture testing tools like ArchUnit.NET) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 83 Td (  or NetArchTest, and separate database schemas\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 70 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.4 0.4 0.4 rg
45 25 Td (INFOSYS & ENTERPRISE .NET INTERVIEW PREPARATION GUIDE  |  Page 100) Tj ET
