BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 528 Td (  segment\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 515 Td (* TraceFlags: `01` \(Sampling flag\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 502 Td (* **OpenTelemetry in .NET**: Built directly into the runtime via) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 491 Td (  `System.Diagnostics.ActivitySource` and `System.Diagnostics.Activity`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 478 Td (* Zero third-party proprietary vendor locking: OpenTelemetry collectors forward traces to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 467 Td (  Jaeger, Zipkin, Dynatrace, Datadog, or Azure App Insights.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 454 Td (* **The Trap**: Generating a new `TraceId` inside each microservice rather than extracting) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 443 Td (  and continuing the incoming `traceparent` context from upstream headers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 430 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How do you inject and propagate the `traceparent` context across) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 419 Td (  asynchronous message brokers like RabbitMQ? *\(Answer: Use OpenTelemetry propagators) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 408 Td (  \(`TraceContextPropagator.Inject`\) to inject trace headers into the RabbitMQ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 397 Td (  `IBasicProperties.Headers` dictionary on publish, and extract them on consumer receive\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 384 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 368 Td (Q109: Idempotent Message Consumers in Event-Driven Systems) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 353 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 340 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 327 Td (* Message brokers provide **At-Least-Once** delivery guarantees. Duplicate messages are) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 316 Td (  inevitable due to network blips, consumer timeouts, or re-deliveries.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 303 Td (* **Idempotency Definition**: An operation can be applied multiple times without changing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 292 Td (  the result beyond the initial application \($f\(f\(x\)\) = f\(x\)$\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 279 Td (* **Implementation Strategies**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 266 Td (* **Idempotency Consumer Table \(Deduplication Gate\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 253 Td (* Every incoming message has a unique `MessageId`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 240 Td (* Consumer begins a local database transaction.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 227 Td (* Tries to insert `MessageId` into a processed messages table with a Primary Key / Unique) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 216 Td (  constraint.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 203 Td (* If insert succeeds: process domain logic, commit transaction, acknowledge broker.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 190 Td (* If insert fails with duplicate key error: skip business logic immediately, acknowledge) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 179 Td (  broker.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 166 Td (* **Natural Business Keys / State Machine Guards**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 153 Td (* `UPDATE Orders SET Status = 'Paid' WHERE Id = @Id AND Status = 'Pending';`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 140 Td (* If the update affects 0 rows because the status is already 'Paid', the message is a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 129 Td (  harmless duplicate; ignore safely.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 116 Td (* **The Trap**: Relying on an in-memory cache \(like Redis\) for idempotency keys without) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 105 Td (  persistent database transaction guarantees. If Redis loses data or evicts the key under) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 94 Td (  memory pressure, duplicate messages will process and corrupt the database.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 81 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What happens if a duplicate message arrives while the first) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 70 Td (  instance is still actively processing? *\(Answer: The unique index insert or a distributed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.4 0.4 0.4 rg
45 25 Td (INFOSYS & ENTERPRISE .NET INTERVIEW PREPARATION GUIDE  |  Page 104) Tj ET
