BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (  pessimistic lock will block or abort the second instance, preventing concurrent duplicate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 769 Td (  execution\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 756 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 740 Td (Q110: API Gateway Pattern: YARP vs Ocelot vs Cloud Native) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 725 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 712 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 699 Td (* The API Gateway acts as the single entry point \(Reverse Proxy\) for all external client) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 688 Td (  traffic entering the microservices cluster.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 675 Td (* **Core Responsibilities**: Request routing, SSL termination, authentication/authorization) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 664 Td (  token validation, rate limiting, request transformation, response aggregation, CORS) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 653 Td (  offloading.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 640 Td (* **Ocelot**: Popular historical .NET open-source gateway. Feature-rich, but slower) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 629 Td (  throughput, higher memory allocations, and slower update cycles.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 616 Td (* **YARP \(Yet Another Reverse Proxy\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 603 Td (* Microsoft's official high-performance reverse proxy toolkit built directly on ASP.NET) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 592 Td (  Core infrastructure and `System.IO.Pipelines`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 579 Td (* Extremely fast, low allocation, handles tens of thousands of requests per second per) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 568 Td (  core.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 555 Td (* Highly extensible via C# code and middleware pipelines; supports dynamic configuration) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 544 Td (  updates without process restart.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 531 Td (* **The Trap**: Implementing heavy business logic or domain aggregations inside the API) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 520 Td (  Gateway. The Gateway becomes a bloated "distributed monolith in disguise" that blocks) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 509 Td (  deployments and creates scaling bottlenecks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 496 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does YARP handle Active and Passive Health Checks for) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 485 Td (  downstream service clusters? *\(Answer: Passive checks evaluate live traffic responses) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 474 Td (  [e.g., consecutive 5xx errors] to pause routing; Active checks probe designated health) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 463 Td (  endpoints on destination servers at configured intervals\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 450 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 434 Td (Q111: Database-per-Service vs Shared Database Anti-Pattern) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 419 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 406 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 393 Td (* **Database-per-Service \(Microservices Rule\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 380 Td (* Each microservice owns its private database. No other service can access the database) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 369 Td (  directly; all interactions must occur through published APIs or event streams.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 356 Td (* Enables loose coupling, independent schema migrations, and technology selection \(polyglot) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 345 Td (  persistence\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 332 Td (* **Shared Database Anti-Pattern**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 319 Td (* Multiple services querying and modifying the same underlying database tables.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 306 Td (* **Catastrophic Flaws**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 293 Td (* Hidden coupling: Changing a column in Service A breaks Service B without compile-time) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 282 Td (  warning.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 269 Td (* Lock contention: Service A's heavy analytical reporting query locks rows required by) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 258 Td (  Service B's high-frequency OLTP path.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 245 Td (* Security boundary failure: Services bypass domain rules and mutate each other's) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 234 Td (  invariants directly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 221 Td (* **The Trap**: Choosing microservices architecture while keeping a single monolithic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 210 Td (  database because "cross-service joins are convenient". You inherit all the operational) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 199 Td (  pain of microservices with none of the autonomy benefits.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 186 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How do you implement a business query that requires data owned by) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 175 Td (  three different microservices? *\(Answer: Using API Composition / Gateway Aggregation for) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 164 Td (  simple cases, or CQRS Read Projections listening to event streams from all three services) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 153 Td (  into a denormalized read view\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 140 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 124 Td (Q112: Distributed Caching Strategies: Cache-Aside vs Write-Through vs Write-Behind) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 109 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 96 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 83 Td (* **Cache-Aside \(Lazy Loading - Most Common\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 70 Td (* Application reads from cache. If hit, returns data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.4 0.4 0.4 rg
45 25 Td (INFOSYS & ENTERPRISE .NET INTERVIEW PREPARATION GUIDE  |  Page 105) Tj ET
