<< /Length 6714 >>
stream
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (* **Phase 2 \(Commit\)**: If all voted YES, coordinator writes commit to log and orders all) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 769 Td (  to commit. If any voted NO, orders all to abort.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 756 Td (* **Critical Flaws**: Blocking protocol. If the coordinator crashes during Phase 2, all) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 745 Td (  participants hold database locks indefinitely, locking tables, exhausting resources, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 734 Td (  stalling the system. Does not scale across modern cloud microservices.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 721 Td (* **Distributed Saga**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 708 Td (* Asynchronous, non-blocking sequence of local transactions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 695 Td (* Resources are committed locally immediately, freeing database locks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 682 Td (* Guarantees **Eventual Consistency** rather than strict ACID isolation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 669 Td (* Solves failure via compensating business actions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 656 Td (* **The Trap**: Recommending 2PC for modern cloud microservices. 2PC violates microservice) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 645 Td (  autonomy, creates tight availability coupling \(availability is the product of all) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 634 Td (  participant availabilities\), and destroys throughput.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 621 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What concurrency isolation anomaly can occur during a Saga) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 610 Td (  execution that 2PC prevents? *\(Answer: Lack of Isolation - intermediate states are visible) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 599 Td (  to concurrent transactions, requiring semantic locks or dirty read countermeasures in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 588 Td (  business logic\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 575 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 559 Td (Q115: Eventual Consistency and Read-Your-Own-Writes Guarantee) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 544 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 531 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 518 Td (* In distributed systems with asynchronous replication \(e.g., Primary database replicating) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 507 Td (  to Read Replicas, or CQRS write-database syncing to read-projections\), updates take time) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 496 Td (  \(replication lag: 50ms - 2s\) to propagate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 483 Td (* **The Problem**: A user edits their profile, clicks "Save", the write goes to the Primary) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 472 Td (  DB. The browser redirects to the profile page, which reads from a lagging Read Replica.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 461 Td (  The user sees their *old* data and panics or submits duplicate requests.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 448 Td (* **Read-Your-Own-Writes Guarantee**: Guarantees that a user will always see updates) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 437 Td (  submitted by themselves, while other users may observe eventual consistency.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 424 Td (* **Implementation Techniques**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 411 Td (* **Session-Based Routing**: Route all read requests for a specific user to the Primary DB) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 400 Td (  for 5-10 seconds immediately following a write mutation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 387 Td (* **Version / Timestamp Tracking**: Server returns a version token or timestamp upon write.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 376 Td (  The client sends this token on subsequent reads; the read replica validates if its local) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 365 Td (  replication state has caught up to that version before responding \(or delegates to primary) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 354 Td (  if behind\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 341 Td (* **Optimistic UI Updates**: Client application state updates immediately in memory upon) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 330 Td (  successful write confirmation without refetching from the replica.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 317 Td (* **The Trap**: Solving replication lag by routing ALL read queries across the entire) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 306 Td (  application to the Primary database, defeating the entire purpose of having read replicas.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 293 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does a CQRS frontend handle eventual consistency when) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 282 Td (  awaiting command completion? *\(Answer: By displaying optimistic UI states or subscribing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 271 Td (  to a SignalR WebSocket notification that pushes the updated read model once the projection) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 260 Td (  finishes processing\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 247 Td (---) Tj ET
