BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 526 Td (Q117: High-Throughput Payment Processing & Idempotency Keys) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 511 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 498 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 485 Td (* **Requirements**: Guarantee zero double-charging under network timeouts, high) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 474 Td (  concurrency, and client retries.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 461 Td (* **Idempotency Key Architecture**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 448 Td (* Client generates a unique UUID `Idempotency-Key` and attaches it to the HTTP header:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 437 Td (  `Idempotency-Key: e3b0c442-...`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 424 Td (* API Gateway / Payment Controller intercepts the request.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 411 Td (* Acquires a distributed lock on the key \(via Redis with 10-second TTL\) to prevent) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 400 Td (  concurrent identical requests from executing in parallel.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 387 Td (* Checks an **Idempotency Store** \(RDBMS or DynamoDB with strong consistency\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 374 Td (* If key exists with status **COMPLETED**: Return cached HTTP response immediately without) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 363 Td (  touching payment gateway.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 350 Td (* If key exists with status **IN_PROGRESS**: Return HTTP 409 Conflict or HTTP 425 Too Early) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 339 Td (  \("Transaction currently processing"\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 326 Td (* If key does not exist: Insert record with status **IN_PROGRESS**, release distributed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 315 Td (  lock, and call third-party payment gateway \(Stripe/Adyen\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 302 Td (* Save gateway transaction ID and full response body into the Idempotency Store with status) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 291 Td (  **COMPLETED**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 278 Td (* Return response to client.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 265 Td (* **The Trap**: Marking the idempotency key as completed *before* receiving confirmation) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 254 Td (  from the payment gateway. If the gateway times out, the client retry will receive a false) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 243 Td (  cached response without payment actually executing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 230 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How do you handle downstream payment gateway webhooks confirming) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 219 Td (  payment when the initial HTTP call timed out? *\(Answer: Payment webhooks carry the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 208 Td (  gateway's transaction ID; worker acquires a distributed lock on the order, checks if) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 197 Td (  already marked paid, updates state idempotently, and publishes an OrderPaid domain) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 186 Td (  event\).*) Tj ET
