BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 496 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 483 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 470 Td (* **Challenge**: WebSockets maintain persistent, stateful TCP connections between the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 459 Td (  client and a specific server instance. In a load-balanced multi-server cluster, User A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 448 Td (  connected to Server 1 cannot natively send messages to User B connected to Server 2.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 435 Td (* **SignalR Backplane Architecture**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 422 Td (* Connects all ASP.NET Core server nodes via a centralized pub/sub backplane \(Azure SignalR) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 411 Td (  Service or Redis Pub/Sub\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 398 Td (* When Server 1 receives a message for User B, it publishes the message to the Redis) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 387 Td (  backplane.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 374 Td (* All server nodes listen to Redis; Server 2 receives the event, identifies that User B is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 363 Td (  connected to its local socket, and pushes the message over the WebSocket connection.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 350 Td (* **Sticky Sessions vs Azure SignalR Service**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 337 Td (* Standard Redis backplane requires Sticky Sessions \(Application Request Routing / ARR) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 326 Td (  Affinity\) during initial HTTP negotiation before WebSocket upgrade.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 313 Td (* **Azure SignalR Service**: Offloads 100% of persistent WebSocket connections to a managed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 302 Td (  cloud service; backend application servers remain completely stateless, eliminating server) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 291 Td (  memory starvation from millions of open sockets.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 278 Td (* **The Trap**: Storing user chat history directly in SignalR memory or trying to broadcast) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 267 Td (  massive binary files over WebSockets. WebSocket channels should only transmit small) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 256 Td (  JSON/Protobuf message payloads; media files should upload directly to Blob storage with) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 245 Td (  URLs shared via chat.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 232 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How do you handle message delivery receipts and offline users in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 221 Td (  a real-time chat architecture? *\(Answer: Write the message to a persistent store) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 210 Td (  [Cassandra/Postgres] before attempting real-time socket delivery; if the recipient's) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 199 Td (  connection ID is absent from presence store, dispatch an asynchronous Push Notification\).*) Tj ET
