BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 418 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 405 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 392 Td (* In distributed databases, central auto-increment integers \(`IDENTITY`\) create single) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 381 Td (  points of failure, scaling bottlenecks, and cross-shard replication conflicts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 368 Td (* **Random UUID \(v4\) Anti-Pattern**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 355 Td (* Completely random 128-bit numbers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 342 Td (* Catastrophic for B-Tree clustered indexes: random values cause continuous **Page) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 331 Td (  Splits**, massive storage fragmentation, and buffer pool churn.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 318 Td (* **Twitter Snowflake Architecture**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 305 Td (* 64-bit integer composed of:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 292 Td (* 1-bit unused \(sign bit\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 279 Td (* 41-bit timestamp \(millisecond precision, providing 69 years of lifespan\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 266 Td (* 10-bit worker/machine ID \(supports 1,024 nodes\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 253 Td (* 12-bit sequence number \(allows 4,096 IDs per millisecond per node\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 240 Td (* **K-Sorted \(Monotonically Increasing\)**: Inserts cleanly at the end of B-Tree indexes) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 229 Td (  with zero page splits. Fits in a native 64-bit SQL `BIGINT`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 216 Td (* **UUID v7 \(RFC 9562 Modern Standard\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 203 Td (* 128-bit time-ordered UUID. Encodes a 48-bit Unix timestamp at the front, followed by) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 192 Td (  random bits. Provides index-friendly sequential clustering while conforming to standard) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 181 Td (  UUID format.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 168 Td (* **The Trap**: Snowflake generator clock drift. If the system clock is set backward by NTP) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 157 Td (  synchronization, the generator can produce duplicate IDs unless it detects drift and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 146 Td (  pauses or uses logical sequence increments.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 133 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: Why is GUID v7 superior to sequential GUIDs generated via) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 122 Td (  `NEWSEQUENTIALID\(\)` in cross-platform .NET applications? *\(Answer: `NEWSEQUENTIALID\(\)` is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 111 Td (  proprietary to SQL Server Windows APIs; GUID v7 can be generated natively in .NET code on) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 100 Td (  Linux, containers, or clients before database insertion\).*) Tj ET
