BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 717 Td (  recommendations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 704 Td (* **Data Structure: Trie \(Prefix Tree\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 691 Td (* Tree where each node represents a character. Walking root to leaf constructs words.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 678 Td (* To avoid traversing the entire subtree on every query, pre-compute and store the **Top 5) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 667 Td (  most frequent search queries** directly at each prefix node.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 654 Td (* Querying prefix "mic" becomes an $O\(L\)$ operation where $L$ is prefix length \(e.g., 3) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 643 Td (  character steps\), returning pre-computed suggestions instantly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 630 Td (* **Storage & Ingestion Pipeline**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 617 Td (* In-memory distributed Trie servers partitioned by prefix character ranges \(`[a-m]`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 606 Td (  `[n-z]`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 593 Td (* Search queries are logged to a Kafka stream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 580 Td (* A distributed streaming job \(Apache Flink or Spark\) aggregates query frequencies over) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 569 Td (  rolling hourly/daily windows and periodically rebuilds/updates the Trie nodes out-of-band.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 556 Td (* Edge Caching: Cache common prefix results \(e.g., single characters "a", "b", "c"\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 545 Td (  directly in Browser Cache or CDN for zero backend latency.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 532 Td (* **The Trap**: Querying SQL databases with `WHERE Keyword LIKE 'mic%' ORDER BY Frequency) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 521 Td (  DESC` in real-time on every keystroke. This causes massive index seek/scan overhead and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 510 Td (  crashes databases under typing bursts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 497 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How do you filter out inappropriate or offensive autocomplete) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 486 Td (  suggestions in real-time? *\(Answer: Maintain an in-memory Bloom Filter or Trie blacklist) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 475 Td (  that purges offensive suggestions before publishing the pre-computed node rankings\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 462 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 446 Td (Q127: Scalable Distributed Logging & Telemetry Pipeline) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 431 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 418 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 405 Td (* **The Antipattern**: Writing logs synchronously over HTTP or direct SQL inserts from) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 394 Td (  inside the web request thread. A slow logging target blocks user API responses.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 381 Td (* **High-Throughput Telemetry Pipeline**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 368 Td (* **In-Process Buffering**: ASP.NET Core applications use non-blocking asynchronous log) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 357 Td (  sinks \(Serilog Async Sink with `Channel<LogEvent>` or `System.Threading.Channels`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 346 Td (  Logging statements push to an in-memory bounded buffer and return immediately \($< 1$) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 335 Td (  microsecond\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 322 Td (* **Log Shippers**: Log events are written to local container stdout / rotated disk files.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 311 Td (  A sidecar agent \(FluentBit, Vector, OpenTelemetry Collector\) scrapes the logs without) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 300 Td (  touching the application runtime.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 287 Td (* **Buffer & Streaming**: Shippers stream events to an Apache Kafka cluster or AWS Kinesis) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 276 Td (  to buffer against massive traffic spikes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 263 Td (* **Storage & Analytics**: Consumers read from Kafka and ingest into an analytical storage) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 252 Td (  engine optimized for time-series text search: Elasticsearch, ClickHouse, or Grafana Loki.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 239 Td (* **Sampling Strategy**: Under extreme traffic, enable probabilistic trace sampling \(e.g.,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 228 Td (  record 100% of errors, but only 1% of successful HTTP 200 requests\) to keep storage costs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 217 Td (  manageable.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 204 Td (* **The Trap**: Using an unbounded in-memory logging buffer. If the log collector drops) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 193 Td (  offline, the buffer grows indefinitely until the application process crashes with an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 182 Td (  `OutOfMemoryException`. Always use a **bounded** channel with drop-oldest or block policy.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 169 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: Why is ClickHouse gaining massive popularity over Elasticsearch) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 158 Td (  for high-volume log storage? *\(Answer: ClickHouse uses columnar compression achieving) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 147 Td (  5-10x higher compression ratios, significantly lower RAM requirements, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 136 Td (  orders-of-magnitude faster SQL analytical queries\).*) Tj ET
