BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 691 Td (* **Triage & Scope**: Verify Gateway vs Application latency. Are requests reaching Kestrel) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 680 Td (  \(check Kestrel access logs\)? If Kestrel response times are $> 30\\text{s}$, the gateway is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 669 Td (  timing out waiting for backend worker threads.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 656 Td (* **Downstream Dependency Check**: Check latency to external dependencies: SQL Server,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 645 Td (  Redis, third-party payment/shipping APIs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 632 Td (* **Connection Pool Exhaustion**: Inspect database connection pools. A missing `await) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 621 Td (  using` or long-running database lock causes connection pool starvation \(`Timeout expired.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 610 Td (  The timeout period elapsed prior to obtaining a connection from the pool`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 597 Td (* **DNS Caching / Resolution Failure**: If using `HttpClient` without `IHttpClientFactory`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 586 Td (  check if internal microservice DNS records shifted during rolling deployment while) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 575 Td (  existing sockets point to terminated pod IPs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 562 Td (* **ThreadPool Starvation**: Check for sync-over-async blocking \(`.Result` / `.Wait\(\)`\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 551 Td (  introduced in the recent release, stalling thread pool expansion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 538 Td (* **Remediation**: Revert deployment immediately via Canary/Blue-Green rollback if p99) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 527 Td (  exceeds SLA; inspect Git diff for blocking calls or missing async database connection) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 516 Td (  disposal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 503 Td (* **The Trap**: Restarting pods blindly without capturing diagnostic artifacts. A restart) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 492 Td (  clears symptoms temporarily but destroys in-memory diagnostic state \(dumps, metrics\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 481 Td (  needed to identify the root cause.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 468 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What command captures an active process memory dump in a Linux) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 457 Td (  Docker container running .NET? *\(Answer: Run `dotnet-dump collect -p <PID>` to generate a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 446 Td (  full core dump for offline SOS/LLDB analysis\).*) Tj ET
