BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 725 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 712 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 699 Td (* **Scenario**: An ASP.NET Core service's memory usage grows continuously over 48 hours) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 688 Td (  until the host OS terminates the container with `OutOfMemoryException` or Kubernetes) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 677 Td (  `OOMKilled`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 664 Td (* **Diagnostic Workflow**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 651 Td (* **Confirm Managed vs Unmanaged**: Run `dotnet-counters monitor`. If `GC Heap Size`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 640 Td (  matches process working set, the leak is in managed memory. If `GC Heap Size` is 200MB but) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 629 Td (  process RAM is 4GB, the leak is unmanaged \(native memory leak via P/Invoke, native) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 618 Td (  handles, or memory profiler hooks\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 605 Td (* **Capture Memory Dump**: Take two dumps separated by 30 minutes \(`dotnet-dump collect`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 592 Td (* **Analyze Dump using SOS**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 579 Td (* `dumpheap -stat`: Displays summary of all objects on the heap sorted by total byte size) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 568 Td (  and count. Look at the top 5 classes consuming memory.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 555 Td (* Identify the offending class \(e.g., `MyCompany.OrderDto` occupying 2.5GB\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 542 Td (* Find instances: `dumpheap -type MyCompany.OrderDto`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 529 Td (* Find the **Root holding them alive**: Run `gcroot <ObjectAddress>` on a sample instance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 516 Td (* SOS prints the GC reachability chain: shows whether it is rooted by a `static) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 505 Td (  Dictionary`, an unclosed event handler, an `AsyncLocal` context, or a Singleton cache) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 494 Td (  without eviction policies.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 481 Td (* **The Trap**: Believing that setting an object to `null` guarantees memory reclamation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 470 Td (  If another long-lived object \(like a static collection or event publisher\) maintains a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 459 Td (  reference to it, the GC will never collect it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 446 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What is the difference between Shallow Size and Retained Size of) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 435 Td (  an object in memory analysis? *\(Answer: Shallow size is the memory consumed by the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 424 Td (  object's direct fields alone; Retained size is the total memory kept alive transitively) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 413 Td (  across the entire object reference graph\).*) Tj ET
