BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 729 Td (Q132: Double Message Processing in Apache Kafka Consumers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 714 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 701 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 688 Td (* **Scenario**: A Kafka consumer worker processes payment records. Occasionally, payments) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 677 Td (  are processed twice, generating duplicate transactions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 664 Td (* **Root Cause: Consumer Group Rebalance caused by `max.poll.interval.ms` Exceeded**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 651 Td (* In Kafka, consumer instances send background heartbeats to the broker coordinator via a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 640 Td (  dedicated background heartbeat thread.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 627 Td (* However, the message processing loop calls `Consume\(\)` / `poll\(\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 614 Td (* If processing a batch of messages takes longer than `max.poll.interval.ms` \(e.g.,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 603 Td (  downstream database slowdown causes batch to take 6 minutes when timeout is 5 minutes\),) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 592 Td (  the Kafka coordinator concludes that the consumer worker has hung or died.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 579 Td (* The coordinator triggers a **Consumer Group Rebalance**, revoking partitions from that) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 568 Td (  consumer and assigning them to another active consumer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 555 Td (* The second consumer begins processing the exact same batch from the last committed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 544 Td (  offset, while the first consumer is *still actively writing* the previous batch to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 533 Td (  database, resulting in duplicate processing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 520 Td (* **Remediation**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 507 Td (* Increase `max.poll.interval.ms` to comfortably exceed worst-case processing latency.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 494 Td (* Reduce `max.poll.records` to consume smaller, faster batches.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 481 Td (* Offload heavy processing to internal worker channels \(`System.Threading.Channels`\) while) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 470 Td (  keeping the Kafka consumption poll loop unblocked.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 457 Td (* Implement strict database **Idempotency Deduplication gates**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 444 Td (* **The Trap**: Assuming that sending background heartbeats prevents Kafka rebalances.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 433 Td (  Heartbeats only prove the process is alive; failing to call `poll\(\)` within) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 422 Td (  `max.poll.interval.ms` explicitly signals that the consumer loop is dead.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 409 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What is the difference between `enable.auto.commit = true` vs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 398 Td (  manual offset committing \(`CommitAsync\(\)`\) in Kafka? *\(Answer: Auto-commit commits offsets) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 387 Td (  periodically in the background regardless of whether processing succeeded, risking message) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 376 Td (  loss upon crash; manual commit ensures offsets commit only after successful business) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 365 Td (  processing\).*) Tj ET
