BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 780 Td (  underlying TCP socket connections across multiple requests while rotating DNS every 2) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 769 Td (  minutes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 756 Td (* **The Trap**: Making `HttpClient` a raw static singleton \(`private static readonly) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 745 Td (  HttpClient _client = new HttpClient\(\)`\) without handling DNS changes. If the target server) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 734 Td (  changes its IP address \(common in cloud deployments\), the static client never refreshes) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 723 Td (  DNS and fails indefinitely.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 710 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does `SocketsHttpHandler.PooledConnectionLifetime` in modern) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 699 Td (  .NET solve both socket exhaustion and DNS refresh issues? *\(Answer: It allows connection) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 688 Td (  pooling across requests while specifying a maximum lifetime [e.g., 2 minutes], after which) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 677 Td (  the connection is closed and a new socket is opened with fresh DNS resolution\).*) Tj ET
