BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 648 Td (Q134: Intermittent TLS / SSL Handshake Failures Under High Load) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 633 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 620 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 607 Td (* **Scenario**: Microservice encounters intermittent `AuthenticationException: The remote) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 596 Td (  certificate is invalid according to the validation procedure` or handshake timeouts) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 585 Td (  strictly during peak traffic hours.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 572 Td (* **Root Causes**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 559 Td (* **Certificate Revocation List \(CRL\) / OCSP Timeout**: By default, during TLS handshake,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 548 Td (  the OS validates certificate revocation by querying external Certificate Authority \(CA\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 537 Td (  CRL/OCSP endpoints over HTTP. Under high outbound connection bursts, if the CA's OCSP) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 526 Td (  responder is slow or rate-limits the requests, handshakes timeout.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 513 Td (* **Ephemeral Port / SNAT Port Exhaustion**: In cloud environments \(Azure App Service / AWS) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 502 Td (  NAT Gateway\), outbound TLS handshakes require available SNAT ports. Exhausting SNAT ports) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 491 Td (  causes dropped packets during the multi-step TLS handshake.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 478 Td (* **Cipher Suite Mismatch / CPU Saturation**: TLS RSA/ECDHE cryptographic handshakes are) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 467 Td (  computationally expensive. Under $100\\%$ CPU saturation, thread scheduling delays cause) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 456 Td (  TLS handshake timeouts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 443 Td (* **Forensic Steps**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 430 Td (* Inspect OS event logs and network traces \(Wireshark / tcpdump\) for `Client Hello` without) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 419 Td (  matching `Server Hello`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 406 Td (* Check SNAT port metrics in cloud monitoring dashboards.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 393 Td (* **The Trap**: Disabling certificate validation in production) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 382 Td (  \(`ServerCertificateCustomValidationCallback =) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 371 Td (  DangerousAcceptAnyServerCertificateValidator`\) to "fix" the error. This exposes the entire) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 360 Td (  enterprise to Man-In-The-Middle \(MITM\) attacks and violates regulatory compliance \(PCI-DSS) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 349 Td (  / HIPAA\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 336 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What is TLS Session Resumption, and how does it reduce TLS) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 325 Td (  handshake overhead? *\(Answer: Allows client and server to cache session keys using Session) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 314 Td (  IDs or TLS Tickets, completing subsequent handshakes in 1 network roundtrip instead of 2) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 303 Td (  without expensive asymmetric crypto\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 290 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 274 Td (Q135: Silent BackgroundService Crashes in ASP.NET Core) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 259 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 246 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 233 Td (* **Scenario**: An ASP.NET Core service's background worker \(`OrderQueueProcessor :) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 222 Td (  BackgroundService`\) mysteriously stops processing items, but the web API continues serving) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 211 Td (  HTTP requests without error. Or conversely, in .NET 6+, the entire application process) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 200 Td (  crashes abruptly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 187 Td (* **The Behavioral Shift in .NET 6+**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 174 Td (* Prior to .NET 6: An unhandled exception inside a `BackgroundService.ExecuteAsync\(\)`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 163 Td (  logged an error, but the background thread died silently while the web host stayed alive.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 152 Td (  The worker stopped processing messages forever \(Zombie process\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 139 Td (* .NET 6+ Default: `HostOptions.BackgroundServiceExceptionBehavior` defaults to `StopHost`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 128 Td (  An unhandled exception inside `ExecuteAsync` logs a critical error and **terminates the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 117 Td (  entire application process** to prevent silent zombie failures.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 104 Td (* **Forensic Diagnosis**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 91 Td (* Check application startup logs and container exit codes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 78 Td (* Inspect logging for `Fatal` error: `The HostOptions.BackgroundServiceExceptionBehavior is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 67 Td (  configured to StopHost. A BackgroundService has thrown an unhandled exception`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.4 0.4 0.4 rg
