BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 153 Td (  container memory limits in cgroups v1/v2.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 140 Td (* If a container is restricted to 1GB RAM on a 64GB host node, **Server GC** by default) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 129 Td (  detects the host's 64GB RAM and provisions memory heaps accordingly, allowing heap) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 118 Td (  allocations to exceed 1GB.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 105 Td (* The Linux kernel OOM Killer detects the container exceeding its cgroup limit and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 94 Td (  immediately terminates the container with `SIGKILL`.) Tj ET
