BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 581.5 Td (Q138: Slow Redis Latency Spikes and Single-Threaded Bottlenecks) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 566.5 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Senior) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 553.5 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 540.5 Td (* **Scenario**: An ASP.NET Core service experiences random 5-second latency spikes querying) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 529.5 Td (  Redis cache. Redis CPU shows high utilization on a single core.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 516.5 Td (* **Redis Architecture Reality**: Redis executes commands on a **single-threaded event) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 505.5 Td (  loop**. If any command takes 3 seconds to execute, ALL other commands from ALL clients) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 494.5 Td (  queue up behind it and block.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 481.5 Td (* **Common Culprits**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 468.5 Td (* **Running `KEYS *` in Production**: Scans the entire Redis keyspace of millions of keys) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 457.5 Td (  in a single blocking call. **Never use `KEYS *` in production; use `SCAN` instead**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 444.5 Td (* **Massive Collections / Big Keys**: Calling `HGETALL`, `SMEMBERS`, or `LRANGE 0 -1` on) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 433.5 Td (  collections containing 500,000 items. Serializing and transmitting megabytes over the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 422.5 Td (  single thread blocks all other operations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 409.5 Td (* **Redis Lua Script Infinite Loop / Heavy Computation**: Running a CPU-intensive script) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 398.5 Td (  that locks the Redis thread.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 385.5 Td (* **Forking Latency on BGSAVE / AOF Rewrite**: When writing RDB snapshots to disk on) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 374.5 Td (  low-memory VMs, the OS `fork\(\)` system call can block the main thread.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 361.5 Td (* **Diagnostic Tools**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 348.5 Td (* Connect to Redis CLI and run: `SLOWLOG GET 10` to view the slowest recent commands and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 337.5 Td (  their execution durations in microseconds.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 324.5 Td (* Run `redis-cli --bigkeys` to scan and detect giant keys.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 311.5 Td (* **The Trap**: Treating Redis like a full relational database and storing multi-megabyte) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 300.5 Td (  complex object graphs in a single cache key.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 287.5 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does Redis 6/7 I/O Threading change the single-threaded) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 276.5 Td (  nature of Redis? *\(Answer: It multi-threads network socket reads and writes, but core) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 265.5 Td (  command execution remains strictly single-threaded\).*) Tj ET
