BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 215.0 Td (* **Operator Precedence Mechanics**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 202.0 Td (* Null-coalescing operator \(`??`\) has lower precedence than relational operators \(`==`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 191.0 Td (  `<`\), but higher precedence than ternary operator \(`?:`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 178.0 Td (* `bool? flag = null; flag == true` evaluates to `false`. In C#, comparing a nullable bool) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 167.0 Td (  `null == true` is `false`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 154.0 Td (* Short-circuiting \(`&&`, `||`\): In `A || B`, if `A` evaluates to `true`, `B` is **never) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 143.0 Td (  evaluated**. If `B` contains a mutating method call \(`Process\(\)`\), that method is silently) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 132.0 Td (  skipped.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 119.0 Td (* **The Trap**: Assuming `if \(boolNullable\)` compiles. In C#, a `bool?` cannot be) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 108.0 Td (  implicitly evaluated as a conditional expression without explicit comparison \(`flag ==) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 97.0 Td (  true`\) or null-coalescing \(`flag ?? false`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 84.0 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: What does `bool? a = null; bool? b = null; Console.WriteLine\(a ==) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 73.0 Td (  b\);` print? *\(Answer: Prints `True`; equality operator on nullable types evaluates `null) Tj ET
