BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 534.0 Td (        result += i.ToString\(\) + ",";) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 524.5 Td (    }) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 508.0 Td (* **The Catastrophe**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 495.0 Td (* Strings are immutable. In every iteration, the runtime allocates a brand-new string) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 484.0 Td (  object on the Managed Heap copying all previous characters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 471.0 Td (* Time Complexity: $O\(N^2\)$ \(copies $1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + N$ characters $\\approx N^2 / 2$) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 460.0 Td (  operations\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 447.0 Td (* Memory: Allocates roughly $\\approx 50\\text{MB}$ of temporary garbage strings for 10,000) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 436.0 Td (  iterations, triggering frequent Gen 0 and Gen 1 GC sweeps.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 423.0 Td (* **Fix**: Use `StringBuilder` with an estimated initial capacity, which manages an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 412.0 Td (  expandable internal buffer in $O\(N\)$ time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 399.0 Td (* **The Trap**: Replacing `string.Concat` with `StringBuilder` for simple single-line) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 388.0 Td (  concatenation \(`string full = first + " " + last;`\). The C# compiler automatically) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 377.0 Td (  transforms single-line `+` expressions into a single `string.Concat\(a, b, c\)` call, which) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 366.0 Td (  is faster and allocates less than instantiating a `StringBuilder`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 353.0 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does `StringBuilder` manage memory when its internal buffer) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 342.0 Td (  capacity is exceeded? *\(Answer: Prior to .NET Core, it reallocated a larger contiguous) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 331.0 Td (  array; modern .NET uses a linked list of chunked character buffers to minimize large array) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 320.0 Td (  reallocations\).*) Tj ET
