BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 594 Td (    public ActionResult GetData\(\) {) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 584.5 Td (        var data = FetchAsync\(\).Result; // Deadlock!) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 575.0 Td (        return View\(data\);) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 565.5 Td (    }) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 556.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 546.5 Td (    private async Task<string> FetchAsync\(\) {) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 537.0 Td (        await Task.Delay\(100\);) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 527.5 Td (        return "Loaded";) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 518.0 Td (    }) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 501.5 Td (* **The Deadlock Mechanics**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 488.5 Td (* Calling thread enters `GetData\(\)`, which has a single-threaded `SynchronizationContext`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 475.5 Td (* `FetchAsync\(\)` begins and hits `await Task.Delay\(100\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 462.5 Td (* The awaiter captures the current `SynchronizationContext`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 449.5 Td (* Calling thread blocks synchronously on `.Result`, waiting for the task to finish.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 436.5 Td (* After 100ms, the delay completes. The continuation attempts to post execution back to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 425.5 Td (  captured `SynchronizationContext` to resume `FetchAsync\(\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 412.5 Td (* However, the `SynchronizationContext` is **blocked**, sitting inside the waiting) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 401.5 Td (  `.Result` call.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 388.5 Td (* **Deadlock**: Calling thread is waiting for the task to complete; the task is waiting for) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 377.5 Td (  the calling thread to free the context.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 364.5 Td (* **Why this does NOT deadlock in ASP.NET Core**: ASP.NET Core does not have a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 353.5 Td (  `SynchronizationContext`; continuations resume on arbitrary ThreadPool threads. \(However,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 342.5 Td (  it still causes ThreadPool Starvation!\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 329.5 Td (* **The Trap**: Believing that because code doesn't deadlock on ASP.NET Core, `.Result` is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 318.5 Td (  safe. It causes catastrophic ThreadPool starvation under production load.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 305.5 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: How does `Task.Run\(\(\) => FetchAsync\(\)\).Result` avoid the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 294.5 Td (  SynchronizationContext deadlock? *\(Answer: `Task.Run` executes the method on a ThreadPool) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 283.5 Td (  thread where `SynchronizationContext.Current` is null, preventing context capture, though) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 272.5 Td (  it still burns an extra thread\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 259.5 Td (---) Tj ET
