BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 742.5 Td (        }) Tj ET
BT /F3 7.5 Tf 0.1 0.15 0.3 rg 52 733.0 Td (    }) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 716.5 Td (* **The Trap**: Candidate believes wrapping `HttpClient` in `using` is standard best) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 705.5 Td (  practice because it implements `IDisposable`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 692.5 Td (* **The Reality**: Each instantiation and disposal burns an OS TCP socket that sits in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 681.5 Td (  `TIME_WAIT` for 2-4 minutes. Under traffic, the system crashes from socket exhaustion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 668.5 Td (* **The Modern Standard**: Inject `IHttpClientFactory` and call `var client =) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 657.5 Td (  _httpClientFactory.CreateClient\(\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 644.5 Td (* **The Trap**: Interviewers testing whether candidates follow standard C# conventions) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 633.5 Td (  \(`using` on `IDisposable`\) blindly without understanding low-level OS network) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 622.5 Td (  abstractions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 609.5 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: Why does `IHttpClientFactory.CreateClient\(\)` create a new) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 598.5 Td (  `HttpClient` instance on each call without causing socket exhaustion? *\(Answer: Because) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 587.5 Td (  the lightweight `HttpClient` wrapper is discarded while the heavy underlying) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 576.5 Td (  `HttpClientHandler` / socket pool is managed and pooled separately\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 563.5 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.2 0.2 0.3 rg 45 547.5 Td (Q155: Code Trap: Tricky Value Tuple vs Anonymous Type Memory and Equality) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 532.5 Td (* **Expected Depth**: Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 519.5 Td (* **Key Answer Points**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 506.5 Td (* **Value Tuples \(`\(int Id, string Name\)`\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 493.5 Td (* Value types \(`struct System.ValueTuple<T1, T2>`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 480.5 Td (* Allocated inline on stack or heap parent; zero GC overhead.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 467.5 Td (* Mutable: fields can be modified \(`tuple.Id = 5`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 454.5 Td (* Value-based equality implemented efficiently via native comparisons.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 441.5 Td (* Field names exist **only at compile time**; erased in IL metadata \(become `Item1`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 430.5 Td (  `Item2`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 417.5 Td (* **Anonymous Types \(`new { Id = 1, Name = "Alice" }`\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 404.5 Td (* Reference types \(`class`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 391.5 Td (* Heap allocated; GC collected.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 378.5 Td (* Completely **immutable** \(read-only properties\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 365.5 Td (* Overrides `Equals` and `GetHashCode` based on properties.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 352.5 Td (* Preserves property names via runtime reflection.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 339.5 Td (* **The Trap**: Returning Value Tuples across assembly or external API boundaries expecting) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 328.5 Td (  property names to be preserved via reflection. The names are compiler metadata; reflection) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 317.5 Td (  inspects them as `Item1` and `Item2`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 304.5 Td (* **Follow-up Question**: When should you choose `record struct` over a Value Tuple?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 293.5 Td (  *\(Answer: When you need domain-specific semantics, explicit method behaviors, interfaces,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 282.5 Td (  or non-destructive mutation via `with` expressions while retaining value type) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 271.5 Td (  performance\).*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 45 258.5 Td (---) Tj ET
