BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 199.5 Td (* **Lead with the Runtime Truth**: Start your answer with what happens in memory and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 188.5 Td (  CLR \(e.g., "Under the hood, this allocates a display class on the managed heap..."\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 175.5 Td (* **Quantify the Trade-offs**: Never declare an absolute "best" pattern. State: "The) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 164.5 Td (  benefit is $O\(1\)$ lookup, but the trade-off is an $O\(N\)$ memory grant that can spill to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 153.5 Td (  tempdb under load.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 140.5 Td (* **Preempt the Interviewer's Trap**: Mention the edge case before they ask \(e.g., "One) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 129.5 Td (  critical trap here is captive dependencies if injected into a singleton..."\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 116.5 Td (* **Tie Directly to Production Incidents**: Reference real telemetry: "In a production) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 105.5 Td (  post-mortem, this manifested as high thread pool queue length and HTTP 504 timeouts on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.15 0.15 rg 52 94.5 Td (  gateway.") Tj ET
